Application Component Report
============================

	Name:            TransferFrom

/*
**      Copyright c 1993 ESCA Corporation  All rights reserved.
**
**      ESCA Corporation proprietary and trade secret information.
**      Do not copy or disclose to third parties without written permission
**      from an officer of ESCA Corporation. 
**
**  Application:    CAC
**  Frame:          TransferFrom 
**
**  Date:           Version  Description
** --------------------------------------------------
**   03/09/93   em   copied from TransferTo
**   04/07/93   em   removed repeated select for ddb
**   05/11/93   em   added parameter to procedure call for transfer job
**   05/26/93   em   added call to originalcard to update feeder info.
**   07/30/93   em   log equipment change on both feeders
**   09/08/93   em   variance fix - set groundon of xferred move to NULL
**   10/04/93   em   performance enhancements, add new print id for destination
**                   feeder
**   11/03/93   em   change sequence of statements when transfer of jobs fails
**   06/15/94   pw   transfer feeder statuses with equipment
**   04/17/94   mts  Added EquipClass to criteria for select from FMS_JobAction.
**   06/16/94   pw   Add NewEquipMove flag so that screen can be used to
**                     select equipment from iso feeders to add moves to a card
**   06/27/94   hlf  add criteria to select from fms_jobaction
**   07/06/94   mts  Loads TypeOfCard FROM table FMS_Card when doing selects.
**   07/07/94   mts  selections from fms_jobaction now look at equipclass heiarchy.
**   10/26/94   hlf  Modify checks/actions to look for moveequipclass
**   03/23/95   pw   Took out dead moves code that was being repeated
**   05/09/95   pw   Take out code that gets rid of 'N' flag.  This is now done in
**                   database procedure.
**   08/08/95   em   When transferring equipment grouped with macro equipment
**                           (like an ATS), the macro equipment is transferred via
**                           a db rule/procedure.  Moves associated with the macro
**                           equipment will be handled in this procedure using the
**                           transfer jobs procedure.                   
**   08/11/95   em   Watch out for macro equip = 0 when transferring moves
**   04/22/96   wc   Added codes to remove any BT statuses
**                   related to this JobClass and equipment
**   12/13/96   em   Call FMS_ManageCardHeader for old and new cards if grounded
**                   equipment has been transferred.
**   03/17/97   jfl  Use MacroGrouper to exclude grouper types.
**   07/24/98   em   Reversed order of equip name and type on log entry.
**   07/25/98   em   Performance; removed NOT IN Grouper sub-select
**   11/22/02   ysp  Load source card's jobs at start. Revised calls to 
**                   FeederStatusUpd. To transfer a job, make a copy of the original
**                   job for the source card and transfer the original to 
**                   the destination card.
**   01/22/03   ysp  Set the ActivityIdentifer to 'T' for the jobs on the destination card. 
**   01/22/03   em   Update activity idnetifier to 'T' only if not 'S'
**   02/03/03   em   If equip being transferred is a Dead Move, update
**                   dead move count for both cards.
**   02/04/03   ysp  Split the transfer of Feeder Statuses into two steps: Undo and Upd 
**                   steps.  This is because the InsertControl of the Job class will update
**                   the statuses in the new card.
**   05/07/03   pkw  Don't allow equipment that has outstanding FOD moves to be transferred. 
**   05/15/06   ysp  Allow the calling environment to pass in SelectEquip.
**   06/02/06   ysp  Return PU_OK if equipment is transferred or, otherwise, PU_CANCEL 
**   07/07/06   ysp  itc 184: added checking if the equip has moves in outstanding operating orders.
**   09/12/06   ysp  Don't allow de-selecting equipment if SelectEquip is passed in.
**   04/17/09   em   When selecting equip for transfer, check if equip is already on the target
**                   feeder and if the equip is the source breaker for the current feeder (KPS). Use 
**                   "IsAssigned" attribute of FMS_Equip class to record and act:
**                       0 = Not on target feeder, complete transfer normally
**                       1 = Is on target feeder, do not add to target or transfer jobs, but delete
**                           from current feeder
**                       2 = Is KPS Source Breaker, same action as =1 plus update primarygrouping
**                           to target feeder.
**   06/18/09   em   Scroll through passed in equip list and retrieve Print ID 
**   08/23/10   em   Exclude 3G Switch from list
**   12/17/12   em   Exclude ATS Grouper from transfer equipment list.
**   07/24/13   ysp  call TransferPhaseCheckEquip after FMS_TransferEquip call is successfully completed
**   09/07/13   pkw  Pair selects of SD-VIS and SD-TRANSF.
**   04/20/16   ysp  For 33kv card, prompt DO to select a portion to transfer equipment to.
**   09/14/16   em   Fix bug calling ManageCardHeader for 33kV feeder portion
**   11/16/16   ysp  Fix transfer problem from ISO when processing FCR work permit return.
**   12/27/17   em   Add handling for DownstreamFrom Selection
**   02/21/18   em   If target feeder has SF6 device, prompt for selection of Downstream From
**   03/12/18   em   Adjusted to prevent KPISO prompt when downstream from exists.
**   05/10/18   em   Corrected infinite loop error on call from FCR Options
**   12/30/19	em	 Include DMEaton in DMSF6 type list
**   03/24/20   em   Add call to MarkDiagramInvalid passing both feeders.
*/
INITIALIZE   
(   C = FMS_Card;		 /* parameter - current card */ 
    SourceFeeder = integer not null; /* parameter - feeder to move equipment from */ 
    NewEquipMove = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /* passed in - optional */
    NewEquip = FMS_Equip;                         /* passed in - optional */
) = 
DECLARE
   ByPassSelection = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;	
   FeederObj = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   FeederName = VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; 
   JobASEClass = Job_ASE DEFAULT NULL;
   Jobs = ARRAY of Job;         /* all jobs for the source card */ 
   SrcCard = FMS_Card;		 /* source card */ 
   i = integer not null;	 /* index variable */ 
   j = integer;		 /* index variable */ 
   k = integer not null;	 /* index variable */ 
   x = integer;
   ngrounds = integer NOT NULL; /* number of grounds for current equipment */ 
   lastjob = integer not null;		 /* stores index of job of piece of equipment */
   status = integer;        	 /* return status variable */ 
   entrymade = integer;	 /* tests if entry was made */ 
   PrimaryGroupingChange = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   SelectCount = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   CurrentRow = INTEGER;
   IDText = varchar(2);
   OrigCard = FrameExec;
   MacroEquip = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   MainFeeder  = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   EquipGrounded = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;   /* Boolean */
   GroundFeeder = ARRAY OF INTEGEROBJECT;
   DeadMove = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;   /* Boolean */
   ControlEntry = NewMoveCard;
   ControlText = VARCHAR(256) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   DSF = ARRAY OF GroupingClass;
   SF6 = ARRAY OF ObjectClass;
   
   SD_Link = PROCEDURE;
   SD_Transfer = PROCEDURE;
ENDDECLARE
BEGIN 
    IF NewEquipMove = TRUE THEN
       NewEquip = NULL;
       CurFrame.WindowTitle = 'Select ISO/Feeder Equipment for moves';
       Field(SelectEquip).IsHighLighted = TRUE;
       Field(SelectEquip[*].newprintid).CurBias = FB_Invisible;
       Field(fromfeeder).TextValue = 'Select Equipment for moves from ISO/Feeder: ';
       Field(tofeeder).CurBias = FB_Invisible;
       Field(originalfeedername).CurBias = FB_Invisible;
       Field(Transfer_Btn).TextLabel = 'OK';
    ENDIF;
    /* Issue message if source feeder is same as current feeder: */ 
    IF (SourceFeeder = C.Feeder) THEN 
      MESSAGE 'Source feeder is same as current feeder!'; 
      RETURN PU_CANCEL; 
    /* Issue message if no feeder was selected: */ 
    ELSEIF (SourceFeeder <= 0) THEN 
      MESSAGE 'No feeder specified.'; 
      RETURN PU_CANCEL; 
    ENDIF; 

    IF NewEquipMove <> TRUE THEN
        OrigCard = OpenFrame OriginalCard (C = C);
    ENDIF;

   /* Get the source  card: */ 
   SELECT :SrcCard.Card = CC.Card, 
          :SrcCard.TypeOfCard = CC.TypeOfCard,
          :SrcCard.SubstationName = CC.SubstationName, 
          :SrcCard.Cutin = CC.Cutin,
          :SrcCard.Cutout = CC.Cutout,
          :SrcCard.StationGround = CC.StationGround,
          :SrcCard.Feeder = CC.Feeder, 
          :SrcCard.DeadMovesTO = CC.DeadMovesTO,
          :SrcCard.Status = CC.Status, 
          :SrcCard.GroundsOn = CC.GroundsOn, 
          :SrcCard.FeederName = CC.FeederName, 
          :SrcCard.NetworkFeeder = CC.NetworkFeeder,
          :SourceFeederName = CC.FeederName  
   FROM   FMS_Card CC,
          SOA_ActiveObject AO 
   WHERE  AO.Object = :SourceFeeder 	AND  
          AO.ObjectToCardLink = 1       AND
          AO.Card = CC.Card;          
   CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;

   IF C.NetworkFeeder = NetworkFeeder$3G THEN
      FeederObj = C.Object[1].Object;
      FeederName = C.Object[1].Name;

      IF C.Object.LastRow() > 1 THEN
         FIELD(NetworkFeeder).ValueList.ChoiceItems.Clear();
         FOR i = 1 TO C.Object.LastRow() DO
            FIELD(NetworkFeeder).ValueList.ChoiceItems[i].EnumValue = C.Object[i].Object;
            FIELD(NetworkFeeder).ValueList.ChoiceItems[i].EnumText = C.Object[i].Name;
         ENDFOR;
         FIELD(NetworkFeeder).CurBias = FB_CHANGEABLE;
         /* OR5.1 FIELD(NetworkFeeder).ColumnWidthCompressed = TRUE; */
         FIELD(NetworkFeeder).UpdChoiceList();
      ENDIF;
      NetworkFeeder = C.Object[1].Object;
      OriginalFeederName = C.Object[1].Name;
   ELSEIF C.NetworkFeeder = NetworkFeeder$33KV THEN
      IF C.TypeOfCard = TypeOfCard$Portion THEN
         SELECT :MainFeeder = C.Feeder,
                :OriginalFeederName = C.FeederName
         FROM   FMS_PortionLink L,
                FMS_Card C
         WHERE  L.PortionCard = :C.Card AND
                L.Card = C.Card;
         CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
      ELSE
         MainFeeder = C.Feeder;
         OriginalFeederName = C.FeederName;
      ENDIF;
      FeederName = OriginalFeederName;
      CALLFRAME PortionFeederDiagram(MainFeeder = MainFeeder,
                                    ClickableList = C.Object,
                                    SelectedPortion =  BYREF(FeederObj),
                                    Title = 'Select a Segment that Equipment will be Transferred to');
      IF FeederObj = 0 THEN
         RETURN;
      ENDIF;
   ELSE
      FeederObj = C.Feeder;
      FeederName = C.FeederName;
      OriginalFeederName = C.FeederName;
   ENDIF;

    entrymade = 0; 
/*
**      Read in the jobs
*/
    IF JobASEClass IS NULL THEN
       JobASEClass = Job_ASE.Create();
    ENDIF;
     
    JobASEClass.Card = SrcCard.Card;
    JobASEClass.ArchiveCard = FALSE;
    JobASEClass.Application = Application$FMS;
    JobASEClass.LoadJobs();
   
    IF JobAseClass.ReturnCode <> 0 THEN
       Message JobAseClass.ErrorMessage;
       RESUME;
    ENDIF;

    Jobs = JobAseClass.J.Duplicate();
    JobASEClass = NULL;

    /*
    ** If SelectEquip is not passed in to this frame. Load all equip
    ** on the source feeder. If SelectEquip is passed in from 
    ** FCR Return Option screen, highlight all rows.
    */
    ByPassSelection = 0;
    IF SelectEquip.LastRow = 0 THEN
       CurFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'load_equip');
    ELSE
       entrymade = 1; 
       ByPassSelection = 1;
       FOR i = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow() DO
          FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Origin).IsReverse = TRUE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Description).IsReverse = TRUE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[i].PrintID).IsReverse = TRUE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipName).IsReverse = TRUE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName).IsReverse = TRUE;
 /*
** Check for DownstreamFrom
*/                       
          j = DSF.LastRow;             
          j = j + 1;
          SELECT :DSF[j].Member = Member,
                 :DSF[j].Grouping = Grouping
          FROM   Udb_Grouping
          WHERE  Member = :SelectEquip[i].Equip AND
                 Relationship = :Interaction$DownstreamFrom;
                  
          // equipment may be members of different portions / feeders.
          IF C.NetworkFeeder > 0 THEN 
            SELECT :SelectEquip[i].Feeder = G.Grouping,
                   :SelectEquip[i].FeederName = O.Name
            FROM   UDB_Grouping G,
                   UDB_Object O
            WHERE G.Member = :SelectEquip[i].Equip AND
                  G.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                  G.GroupingType IN (SELECT Type 
                                     FROM   UDB_ExtendedType
                                     WHERE  SuperType = :Type$Feeder) AND
                  G.Grouping = O.Object;
          ELSE
            SelectEquip[i].Feeder = SourceFeeder;
            SelectEquip[i].FeederName = SourceFeederName;
          ENDIF;
          
          SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID = SelectEquip[i].PrintID;
          IF SelectEquip[i].PrintID = '' THEN  /* Confirm PrintID for all cases */
             SELECT :SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID = Reference,
                    :SelectEquip[i].PrintID = Reference
             FROM   Udb_Grouping
             WHERE  Grouping = :SourceFeeder AND
                    Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                    Member = :SelectEquip[i].Equip;
          ENDIF;  
       ENDFOR;
    ENDIF;
END;

ON SETVALUE NetWorkFeeder =
BEGIN
   FeederObj = FIELD(NetworkFeeder).CurEnumValue;
   FeederName = FIELD(NetworkFeeder).CurEnumText;
   OriginalFeederName = FIELD(NetworkFeeder).CurEnumText;

   IF (SourceFeeder = FeederObj) THEN 
      MESSAGE 'Source feeder is same as current feeder!'; 
      RETURN PU_CANCEL;
   ENDIF; 
END;


ON UserEvent 'load_equip' =
BEGIN
   SelectEquip.Clear();	/* Clear out storage */ 
   i = 1;

   IF SrcCard.NetworkFeeder = NetworkFeeder$33KV THEN
      REPEATED
      SELECT  :SelectEquip[i].Equip = O2.Object,  
              :SelectEquip[i].EquipName = O2.Name, 
              :SelectEquip[i].EquipClass  = O2.Type, 
              :SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName  = O2.TypeName, 
              :SelectEquip[i].PrintID = G2.Reference, 
              :SelectEquip[i].Origin = O2.OwnerNumber, 
              :SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID = G2.Reference, 
              :SelectEquip[i].Description = O2.Description,
              :SelectEquip[i].IsAssigned = 0,  
              :SelectEquip[i].Feeder = G1.Member
      FROM    UDB_Grouping G1,
              Udb_Grouping G2,
              Udb_Object O2
      WHERE   G1.Grouping = :SourceFeeder AND
              G1.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
              G1.MemberType IN (SELECT Type 
                                FROM   Udb_ExtendedType
                                WHERE  SuperType = :Type$33KVPortion) AND
              G1.Member = G2.Grouping AND	
              G2.Member = O2.Object AND 
              G2.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
              G2.MemberType IN (SELECT Type
                               FROM   Udb_ExtendedType
                               WHERE  SuperType = :Type$Switch) AND
              G2.MemberType NOT IN (SELECT Type
                                   FROM   Udb_ExtendedType
                                   WHERE  SuperType IN (:Type$Grouper,:Type$3GSwitch))
      ORDER BY PrintID, EquipName, Equip
      BEGIN 
         SelectEquip[i].FeederName = SourceFeederName;
         i = i + 1; 
      END; 

      /* remove duplicate interrupter switches because they are members of two portions.
      */
      i = SelectEquip.LastRow;
      WHILE i >=2 DO
         IF SelectEquip[i-1].Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip THEN
            SelectEquip.RemoveRow(RowNumber = i);
         ENDIF;
         i = i - 1;
      ENDWHILE;
   ELSE
       /* Load equipment list for source feeder: */
       SELECT :SelectEquip[i].Equip = O.Object, 
              :SelectEquip[i].EquipName = O.Name, 
              :SelectEquip[i].EquipClass  = O.Type,
              :SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName  = O.TypeName,
              :SelectEquip[i].PrintID = G.Reference, 
              :SelectEquip[i].Origin = O.OwnerNumber, 
              :SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID = G.Reference, 
              :SelectEquip[i].Description = O.Description,
              :SelectEquip[i].IsAssigned = 0, 
              :SelectEquip[i].Feeder = G.Grouping
       FROM   Udb_Object O, 
              Udb_Grouping G 
       WHERE  G.Grouping = :SourceFeeder AND 
              G.Member = O.Object AND 
              G.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
              G.MemberType IN (SELECT Type
                                   FROM   Udb_ExtendedType
                                   WHERE  SuperType = :Type$Switch) AND
              G.MemberType NOT IN (SELECT Type
                                FROM   Udb_ExtendedType
                                WHERE  SuperType IN (:Type$Grouper,:Type$3GSwitch))  
       ORDER BY PrintID, EquipName
       BEGIN
         SelectEquip[i].FeederName = SourceFeederName;
         i = i + 1;
       END; 
   ENDIF;
   CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
END; 

/* 
**  Handle an equipment selection from the list:  
*/ 
ON ChildEntry SelectEquip[*].Origin,
ON ChildEntry SelectEquip[*].Description,
ON ChildEntry SelectEquip[*].PrintID,
ON ChildEntry SelectEquip[*].EquipName,
ON ChildEntry SelectEquip[*].EquipClassName = 
BEGIN 
    IF (CurFrame.ReasonCode <> RC_MOUSECLICK) THEN
        RESUME;
    ENDIF;
/*
** if SelectEquip is passed in, don't allow de-selection of equipment.
*/
    IF ByPassSelection = 1 THEN
       RESUME;
    ENDIF;

    entrymade = 1; 
    IF NewEquipMove <> TRUE THEN
       IF (FIELD(SelectEquip[].Description).IsReverse = FALSE) THEN
          /*
          ** Check if equip has a move that was downloaded to an Operating Order or FOD Order
          */
          status = CALLPROC CheckOutstandingEquip(Equip = SelectEquip[].Equip);

          IF status = PU_CANCEL THEN
             MESSAGE 'Equipment ' +
                SelectEquip[].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                SelectEquip[].EquipName +
               ' has a move or moves that were downloaded to an order. ' + 
               ' This equipment cannot be transferred ' +
               'until the order processing is complete and confirmed.';
             RESUME;
          ENDIF;

          SELECT :SelectEquip[].IsAssigned = 1
          FROM   Udb_Grouping 
          WHERE  Member = :SelectEquip[].Equip AND
                 Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                 Grouping = :FeederObj;

          IF SelectEquip[].IsAssigned = 1 THEN
             SELECT :SelectEquip[].IsAssigned = 2
             FROM   Udb_Grouping 
             WHERE  Member = :SelectEquip[].Equip AND
                    Relationship = :Interaction$SourceBreaker AND
                    Grouping = :SelectEquip[].Feeder;
          ENDIF;

          FIELD(SelectEquip[].Origin).IsReverse = TRUE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[].Description).IsReverse = TRUE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[].PrintID).IsReverse = TRUE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipName).IsReverse = TRUE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipClassName).IsReverse = TRUE;

          CALLPROC SD_Link(Object = SelectEquip[].Equip,
                       IsReverse = TRUE,
                       Type = SelectEquip[].EquipClass);
/*
** Check for DownstreamFrom
*/                       
          i = DSF.LastRow;             
          i = i + 1;
          SELECT :DSF[i].Member = Member,
                 :DSF[i].Grouping = Grouping
          FROM   Udb_Grouping
          WHERE  Member = :SelectEquip[].Equip AND
                 Relationship = :Interaction$DownstreamFrom;
        ELSE
          FIELD(SelectEquip[].Origin).IsReverse = FALSE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[].Description).IsReverse = FALSE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[].PrintID).IsReverse = FALSE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipName).IsReverse = FALSE;
          FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipClassName).IsReverse = FALSE;
    
          CALLPROC SD_Link(Object = SelectEquip[].Equip,
                       IsReverse = FALSE,
                       Type = SelectEquip[].EquipClass);
/*
** Remove from DownstreamFrom if it is there
*/                       
          i = DSF.LastRow;
          WHILE i > 0 DO
            IF DSF[i].Member = SelectEquip[].Equip THEN
               DSF.RemoveRow (RowNumber = i );
               ENDLOOP;
            ENDIF;
            i = i - 1;
          ENDWHILE;
        ENDIF; 
    ENDIF; 
END; 

ON Click Cancel_Btn,
ON Click Transfer_Btn =
BEGIN
/*
**  Check to see whether or not the original card data needs to be saved.
*/
    IF (Curframe.TriggerField = FIELD(Transfer_Btn)) THEN
        OrigCard.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'UpdateCard');
        Curframe.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'ContinueTransfer_Btn');
    ELSE
        OrigCard.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'ExitFrame');
        Curframe.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'ContinueCancel_Btn');
    ENDIF;
END;

/* 
**  Handle a TRANSFER click:  
*/ 
ON UserEvent 'ContinueTransfer_Btn' =
DECLARE

ENDDECLARE 
BEGIN 
   IF (entrymade != 1) THEN
       message 'You must first select a piece of equipment.';
       RESUME;
   ENDIF;

   IF NewEquipMove = TRUE THEN
      CurrentRow = Field(SelectEquip).ActiveRow;
      IF CurrentRow = 0 THEN
         message 'Please select the piece of equipment again and then hit OK';
      ELSE
         IDText = CALLFRAME GenericEntry ( 
                  PromptPhrase = 'Please enter ID for new Equipment',
                  PhraseLength = 2);

         SelectEquip[CurrentRow].PrintID = IFNULL(IDText,'');
         NewEquip = SelectEquip[CurrentRow].Duplicate();
         Return PU_OK;
      ENDIF;
   ELSE
      DeadMove = FALSE;
      EquipGrounded = FALSE;   
      i = 1;
      WHILE (i <= SelectEquip.LastRow()) DO 

         IF (FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Description).IsReverse = TRUE) THEN

           entrymade = 2; 

      	   /* Get number of grounds for current piece of equipment: */ 
           ngrounds = 0; 
      	   SELECT :ngrounds = O.StatusCount
       	   FROM   FMS_ObjectStatus O 
       	   WHERE  O.Object = :SelectEquip[i].Equip AND 
       	          O.Status = :Status$Ground; 
           CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
           IF ngrounds > 0 THEN
              EquipGrounded = TRUE;
              k = GroundFeeder.Find(AttributeName = 'Value',
                                    Value = SelectEquip[i].Feeder);
              IF k = ER_ROWNOTFOUND THEN
                 GroundFeeder.InsertRow (RowNumber = 1);
                 GroundFeeder[1].Value = SelectEquip[i].Feeder;
              ENDIF; 
           ENDIF;

           /* Is the source Feeder the PrimaryGrouping for the Equipment? */
           PrimaryGroupingChange = 0;
           SELECT :PrimaryGroupingChange = COUNT(*)
           FROM   Udb_Object
           WHERE  Object = :SelectEquip[i].Equip AND
                 (PrimaryGrouping = :SelectEquip[i].Feeder OR
                  PrimaryGrouping IN (SELECT Object
                                            FROM   Udb_Object
                                            WHERE  Type = :Type$TempSubstation));
           CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;

           /* Undo feeder statuses from the source feeder */
           status = CALLPROC FeederStatusUndo(Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                                             SourceCard = SrcCard,
                                             J = Jobs,
                                             Action = 'Xfer');
           IF (status = PU_CANCEL) THEN 
              CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
              MESSAGE 'Unable to drop feeder statuses from the source card';
              ENDLOOP;
              RESUME; 
           ENDIF;
           CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
 
       IF SelectEquip[i].IsAssigned >= 1 THEN  /* Just delete from current feeder*/

           status = Udb_GroupingDel (Grouping = SelectEquip[i].Feeder,
                                     Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf,
                                     Member = SelectEquip[i].Equip);
           IF status > 0 THEN
              CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
              Message 'Unable to remove ' +
                  SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                  SelectEquip[i].EquipName + ' from current feeder.';

           ELSEIF SelectEquip[i].IsAssigned >= 2 THEN  /* Reset primary grouping to target feeder */
               status = CALLPROC Udb_ObjectUpd (
                                       Object = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                                       PrimaryGrouping = FeederObj,
                                       Type = SelectEquip[i].EquipClass,
                                       Name = SelectEquip[i].EquipName);
               IF status < 0 THEN
                  CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                  Message 'Unable to primary group ' +
                     SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                     SelectEquip[i].EquipName + ' to destination feeder.';
               ENDIF;
           ENDIF;
           CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;

       ELSE

           /* Transfer equip and grounds to the new Feeder */ 
           status = CALLPROC FMS_TransferEquip  
                  (Feeder      = SelectEquip[i].Feeder,  
                   DestFeeder  = FeederObj, 
                   Equip       = SelectEquip[i].Equip, 
                   NewPrintID  = SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID, 
                   MemberOfRelation  = Interaction$MemberOf, 
                   SourcePosRelation = Interaction$SourcePosition,
                   EquipGrounds = ngrounds,
                   GroundStatus = Status$Ground,
                   NewPrimaryGrouping = PrimaryGroupingChange);
 
           IF status <> 0 THEN
             CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
             Message 'Transfer of ' + SelectEquip[i].PrintID + '  ' +
                     SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                     SelectEquip[i].EquipName + ' failed.';

             /* Transfer feeder statuses back to old feeder */
             status = CALLPROC FeederStatusUpd(Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                                               DestCard = SrcCard,
                                               J = Jobs,
                                               Action = 'Xfer');
             IF (status = PU_CANCEL) THEN 
                CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                MESSAGE 'Unable to reverse feeder status transfer after equipment ' +
                        'transfer failed.  Feeder Statuses has been transferred, ' +
                        'but the equipment has not.  Contact FMS technical ' +
                        'support.';
                ENDLOOP;
                RESUME; 
             ENDIF;
             CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;

             CurFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'load_equip');
             ENDLOOP;
           ELSE
             CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
             
             CALLPROC TransferPhaseCheckEquipment (
                   Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                   EquipName = SelectEquip[i].EquipName,
                   OldFeeder 	= SelectEquip[i].Feeder,
                   OldFeederName = SourceFeederName,  
                   NewFeeder 	= FeederObj,
                   NewFeederName = OriginalFeederName);
           ENDIF;		      
/*
**   Check if equipment is attached to a macro equipment.  If it is, we will
**   have to transfer moves for that equip as well.
*/
           MacroEquip = 0;
           REPEATED 
           SELECT :MacroEquip = G.Grouping
           FROM   Udb_Grouping G,
                  Udb_ExtendedType ET
           WHERE  G.GroupingType    = ET.Type AND
                  ET.SuperType    = :Type$Switch AND
                  G.Relationship  = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                  G.Member        = :SelectEquip[i].Equip; 
           CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
/*
** Transfer and manipulate jobs 
*/
           j = 1;
           WHILE j <= Jobs.LastRow() DO  
             IF (Jobs[j].Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip OR
                  (Jobs[j].Equip = MacroEquip AND MacroEquip > 0)) AND
                  Jobs[j].Status = '' THEN
 
   	       IF ( (Jobs[j].TOIssued IS NULL) OR   
                    (Jobs[j].TOComplete IS NULL) OR   
                    (Jobs[j].RSIssued   IS NULL) OR   
                    (Jobs[j].RSComplete IS NULL)   ) THEN
  
                 /* Blank out any NULL times: */
                 IF (Jobs[j].TOIssued IS NULL) THEN 
                    Jobs[j].ToIssued = ' '; 
                 ENDIF; 
                 IF (Jobs[j].TOComplete IS NULL) THEN 
                    Jobs[j].TOComplete = ' '; 
                 ENDIF; 
                 IF (Jobs[j].RSIssued IS NULL) THEN 
                    Jobs[j].RSIssued = ' '; 
                 ENDIF; 
                 IF (Jobs[j].RSComplete IS NULL) THEN  
                    Jobs[j].RSComplete = ' '; 
                 ENDIF; 
              
                 IF Jobs[j].MoveType = 'Dead' AND DeadMove = FALSE THEN
                    DeadMove = TRUE;
                 ENDIF;

                 Jobs[j].Response = 'Xfer to ' + FeederName; 
                 Jobs[j].Status = Job$Xfer; 
                 Jobs[j].GroundOn = NULL;
                 Jobs[j].MoveFGColor = CC_BLACK;
              
                 /* Transfer the job from the source card to the current card.  A copy
                    of the job stays with the source card. */ 
                 status = CALLPROC SOA_TransferEquipJob 
                    ( Card       = SrcCard.Card,
                      Job        = Jobs[j].Job, 
                      Response   = Jobs[j].Response, 
                      Status     = Jobs[j].Status, 
                      TOIssued   = Jobs[j].TOIssued, 
                      TOComplete = Jobs[j].TOComplete, 
                      RSIssued   = Jobs[j].RSIssued, 
                      RSComplete = Jobs[j].RSComplete,
                      GroundOn   = Jobs[j].GroundOn,
                      MoveFGColor= Jobs[j].MoveFGColor
                    ); 

                 IF (status <> 0) THEN 
                    CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;

                    Message 'Unable to transfer moves related to ' + 
                          SelectEquip[i].PrintID + '  ' +
                          SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                          SelectEquip[i].EquipName + 
                      ' . Equipment transfer failed.';
                  
                    status = CALLPROC FMS_UndoTransferEquip  
                             (SourceFeeder = SelectEquip[i].Feeder,  
                              Feeder       = FeederObj, 
                              Equip        = SelectEquip[i].Equip, 
                              OldPrintID   = SelectEquip[i].PrintID, 
                              MemberOfRelation  = Interaction$MemberOf, 
                              SourcePosRelation = Interaction$SourcePosition,
                              EquipGrounds = ngrounds,
                              GroundStatus = Status$Ground);

                    IF status <> 0 THEN
                       CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                       Message 'Unable to reverse equipment transfer after move ' +
                         'transfer failed.  Equipment has been transferred, ' +
                         'but their moves have not.  Contact FMS technical ' +
                         'support.';
                       ENDLOOP;
                       RESUME; 
                    ENDIF; 
                    CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;

                    status = CALLPROC FeederStatusUpd(Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                                                DestCard = SrcCard,
                                                J = Jobs,
                                                Action = 'Xfer');
                    IF (status = PU_CANCEL) THEN 
                       CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                       MESSAGE 'Unable to reverse feeder status transfer after move ' +
                          'transfer failed.  Feeder Statuses have been dropped from ' +
                          'the source card. Equipment and moves have not been transferred. ' +
                          ' Contact FMS technical support.';
                       ENDLOOP;
                       RESUME; 
                    ENDIF;
                    CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;

                    CurFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'load_equip');
                    ENDLOOP;
                 ENDIF;
                 CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;

                 /*      
                 **  Establish control entry for destination card linking to the original move
                 */       
                 ControlEntry.Card = C.Card;
                 ControlEntry.Seq = 0;
                 ControlEntry.SwitchingItem = 0;
                 ControlEntry.Application = Application$FMS;
                 ControlEntry.MoveEquipClass = Jobs[j].MoveEquipClass;
                 ControlEntry.PrintID = SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID;
                 ControlEntry.StepHeading = Jobs[j].StepPair;
                 ControlEntry.StepLevel = 0;
                 ControlEntry.TypeOfCard = C.TypeOfCard; 
         
                 Status = Jobs[j].InsertControl (
                                  ControlEntry = ControlEntry
                                 ,InitiatingCard = C.Card
                                 ,TransferFlag = TRUE
                                 ,SingleFeederOnly = TRUE
                                  );

                 IF Status = PU_CANCEL THEN
                    MESSAGE 'Procedure:TransferFrom; Unable to establish ' +
                             'insert move control for the current card.' + 
                             SelectEquip[i].EquipName + ' has been transferred, ' +
                             'the moves have not - contact Tech Support';
                    ENDLOOP;
                    RESUME; 
                 ENDIF;  

                 /* set the ActivityIdentifier to 'T' */
                 IF Jobs[j].ActivityIdentifier <> 'S' THEN
                    CALLPROC SOA_JobActivityIDUpd (Job = Jobs[j].Job,
                                               ActivityIdentifier = 'T');
                 ENDIF;
                 /*
                 ** Change Control Card for move if controlled by the previous card
                 */
                 IF Jobs[j].ControlCard = SrcCard.Card THEN
                    status = CALLPROC SOA_JobControlCardUpd (
                                            Job = Jobs[j].Job,
                                            Card = C.Card);
                    IF status <> 0 THEN
                       CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                       MESSAGE 'Unable to change control card for move ' + 
                               VARCHAR(Jobs[j].Job) + ' to the current card. ' + 
                               'Move might not be accessible - contact Tech Support.';
                    ENDIF;
                 ENDIF;
                 CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
               ENDIF;
             ENDIF;
             j = j + 1; 
           ENDWHILE; 
/*
** Update  the destination Card
*/        
           status = CALLPROC FMS_DestCardUpdate (
                                  DestinationCard = C.Card,
                                  Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip);
 
           IF status < 0 THEN
               CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
               Message 'Unable to update current card to reflect ' +
                       'move transfers related to transferred ' +
                       'equipment.';
               ENDLOOP;
               RESUME;
           ELSE
               CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
               IF status > 0 THEN
                  message 'Because duplicate moves were transferred with this equipment,  ' +
                         'existing protection move links could not be resolved/' +
                         'transferred.  Please review your protection move links ' +
                         'on the Work Permits screen.';
               ENDIF;
           ENDIF;

           IF MacroEquip > 0 THEN
               status = CALLPROC FMS_DestCardUpdate (
                                  DestinationCard = C.Card,
                                  Equip = MacroEquip);
 
               IF status < 0 THEN
                  CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                  Message 'Unable to update current card to reflect ' +
                       'move transfers related to macro equipment.';
                  ENDLOOP;
                  RESUME;
               ELSE
                  CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
                  IF status > 0 THEN
                     message 'Because duplicate moves were transferred with macro equipment,  ' +
                         'existing protection move links could not be resolved/' +
                         'transferred.  Please review your protection move links ' +
                         'on the Work Permits screen.';
                  ENDIF;
               ENDIF;
           ENDIF;
/*
** Remove any BT statuses
** related to this Jobclass and equipment
*/
           j = Jobs.LastRow();
           WHILE ( j  > 0 ) DO

             IF Jobs[j].StepPair = StepHeading$OTW THEN

               IF Jobs[j].equip = SelectEquip[i].equip THEN

                  x = CALLPROC FMS_FromWorkStatusDel
                     (JobClass = Jobs[j].JobClass,
                      Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                      Job = 0,
                      Status = Status$BT,
                      Feeder = SelectEquip[i].Feeder);

                  IF x < 0 THEN
                     CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                     Message 'Unable to clear BT feeder status.  Feeder Status List may be incorrect.';
                  ELSE
                     CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
                  ENDIF;                  

               ENDIF;   

             ENDIF;

             j = j - 1 ;
           ENDWHILE;
      ENDIF;  /*KPS SB*/

           /* Log the transfer of equipment */ 
           CALLPROC SOA_LogIns 
	               ( Card     = C.Card, 
	                 Job      = NULL,
                         Time     = Date('now'),
                         UserName = UserName,        
	                 Item     = 'Xfr Equip', 
	                 Old  = SelectEquip[i].PrintID + ' ' +
                                SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                                SelectEquip[i].EquipName,
	                 New  = 'From ' + :SelectEquip[i].FeederName
                          	 ); 
           CALLPROC SOA_LogIns
	               ( Card     = SrcCard.Card, 
	                 Job      = NULL,        
                         Time     = Date('now'),
                         UserName = UserName,        
	                 Item     = 'Xfr Equip', 
	                 Old  = SelectEquip[i].PrintID + ' ' +
                                SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                                SelectEquip[i].EquipName,
	                 New  = 'To ' + FeederName 
                          	 ); 
           CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
           /*
           **  Transfer SD Link if necessary.
           */
           CALLPROC SD_Transfer (SE = SelectEquip[i].Duplicate());
         ENDIF; 
        
         i = i + 1; 
      ENDWHILE;  
      CALLPROC MarkDiagramInvalid (Feeder = SourceFeeder, Feeder2 = FeederObj);
/*
**    Handle remaining downstream from, look for Grouper on Target
*/   
      i = 1;
      SF6.Clear();
      REPEATED
      SELECT :SF6[i].PrimaryGrouping = O1.Object,
          :SF6[i].PrimaryGroupingName = O1.Name,
          :SF6[i].Object = O2.Object,
          :SF6[i].Name = O2.Name,
          :SF6[i].TypeName = O2.TypeName,
          :SF6[i].Description = O2.Description
      FROM   Udb_Object O1,
          Udb_Object O2,
          Udb_Grouping G
      WHERE  O2.Type IN       (SELECT Type
                            FROM  Udb_ExtendedType
                            WHERE  SuperType IN (:Type$DMSF6Switch,
                                                 :Type$DMEaton,
                                                 :Type$KPS,
                                                 :Type$FastSw,
                                                 :Type$DMVac) ) AND
          O2.Object = G.Member AND
          G.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
          G.Grouping = :FeederObj AND
          G.Grouping = O1.Object
      ORDER BY 2,5,4
      BEGIN 
         i = i + 1;
      END;

      FOR i = 1 TO DSF.LastRow DO
/*
** Find index in SelectList
*/
         FOR k = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow DO
             IF SelectEquip[k].Equip = DSF[i].Member THEN
                ENDLOOP;
             ENDIF;
         ENDFOR;
         
         j = 0;
         SELECT :j = Member
         FROM   Udb_Grouping 
         WHERE  Grouping = :FeederObj AND
                Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                Member = :DSF[i].Grouping;
/*
**    If it doesn't exist, delete it and look for another option
*/        
         IF j = 0 THEN
            x = CALLPROC Udb_GroupingDel (
                             Grouping = DSF[i].Grouping,
                             Relationship = Interaction$DownstreamFrom,
                             Member = DSF[i].Member);
            IF x < 0 THEN
               CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
               CALLPROC TraceError (UserMessage = '',
                                    TraceMessage = 'TransferFrom: Unable to clear DownStreamFrom ' +
                                                 'for Object ' + VARCHAR(DSF[i].Member));
            ELSE
               CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
               IF SF6.LastRow > 0 THEN
                  CALLFRAME KPISOSectionPrompt (Feeder = FeederObj, 
                                       FeederName = FeederName,
                                       SF6 = SF6,
                                       Equip = DSF[i].Member,
                                       EquipName = SelectEquip[k].EquipName,
                                       EquipPrintID = SelectEquip[k].PrintID,
                                       EquipTypeName = SelectEquip[k].EquipClassName
                                      );
                  SelectEquip[k].IsAssigned = 99;
               ENDIF;
            ENDIF; 
         ELSE                 
            SelectEquip[k].IsAssigned = 99;
         ENDIF;
      ENDFOR;     
/*
** If device downstreamfrom was not already handled and target feeder has SF6 option, then
** prompt to add Downstream From relationship.
*/      
      IF SF6.LastRow > 0 THEN
         FOR k = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow DO
            IF SelectEquip[k].IsAssigned <> 99 AND FIELD(SelectEquip[k].Description).IsReverse = TRUE THEN
                   CALLFRAME KPISOSectionPrompt (Feeder = FeederObj, 
                                       FeederName = FeederName,
                                       SF6 = SF6,
                                       Equip = SelectEquip[k].Equip,
                                       EquipName = SelectEquip[k].EquipName,
                                       EquipPrintID = SelectEquip[k].PrintID,
                                       EquipTypeName = SelectEquip[k].EquipClassName
                                      );
            ENDIF;
         ENDFOR;
      ENDIF;
/*
**    Adjust card header for both cards involved, just in case ground move or
**    dead move was transferred.
*/
      IF EquipGrounded = TRUE THEN
         FOR k = 1 TO GroundFeeder.LastRow DO
            CALLPROC FMS_ManageCardHeader (OptionalFeeder = GroundFeeder[k].Value, Equip = 0);
            CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
         ENDFOR;
         CALLPROC FMS_ManageCardHeader (OptionalFeeder = FeederObj, Equip = 0);
         CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
      ENDIF;

      IF DeadMove = TRUE THEN
         status = CALLPROC FMS_DeadMoveCount (Card = C.Card);
         IF status <> 0 THEN
            CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
           MESSAGE 'Dead Move Count on Old Card may not be correct due to an ' +
                 'error';
         ELSE
            CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
         ENDIF;
      ENDIF;

      IF entrymade < 2 THEN
         Message 'No Equipment to transfer.';
         RESUME;
      ELSE
         FCFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'load_jobs');

         ControlText = VARCHAR(SrcCard.Card) + ';' + UserName + ';';
         CALLPROC DDB_RaiseDBEvent ( DBEventName = 'SOA_NewJobOnCard', 
                                     DBEventText = ControlText); 
         CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
      ENDIF;
      RETURN PU_OK; 
   ENDIF;  
END; 
/* 
**  Handle a Cancel click:  
*/ 
ON UserEvent 'ContinueCancel_Btn' = 
BEGIN 
   IF (entrymade > 0) AND NewEquipMove <> TRUE THEN 
      IF (CurFrame.ConfirmPopup(messagetext= 
	      'Equipment will not be transferred.  Continue?') = PU_OK) THEN 
         RETURN PU_CANCEL;  
      ENDIF; 
   ELSE 
      RETURN PU_CANCEL;  
   ENDIF; 
END; 

/* 
**  Handle the Close Window Command: 
*/ 
ON WINDOWCLOSE = 
BEGIN 
	RESUME; 
END; 

PROCEDURE SD_Link (
   Object    = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   IsReverse = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   Type      = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
) =
DECLARE
   i         = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   SDObject  = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
ENDDECLARE
BEGIN 
   /*
   **  Check to see if this is a type we are interested in.
   */
   SDObject = 0;
   IF Type = Type$StepDown THEN  /* SD-TRANSF */
      /*
      **  Find paired piece of equipment
      */
      SELECT :SDObject = G.Member
      FROM    Udb_Grouping G
      WHERE   G.Grouping = :Object AND
              G.Relationship = :Interaction$LocatedWith AND
              G.MemberType = :Type$SDVIS;
   ELSEIF Type = Type$SDVIS THEN
      /*
      **  Find paired piece of equipment
      */
      SELECT :SDObject = G.Grouping
      FROM    Udb_Grouping G
      WHERE   G.Member = :Object AND
              G.Relationship = :Interaction$LocatedWith AND
              G.GroupingType = :Type$StepDown;
   ENDIF;
   
   IF SDObject <> 0 THEN 
      FOR i = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow DO
         IF SelectEquip[i].Equip = SDObject THEN
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Origin).IsReverse = IsReverse;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Description).IsReverse = IsReverse;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].PrintID).IsReverse = IsReverse;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipName).IsReverse = IsReverse;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName).IsReverse = IsReverse;
 
            RETURN;
         ENDIF;
      ENDFOR;
   ENDIF;
          
   RETURN;
END;

PROCEDURE SD_Transfer (
   SE = FMS_Equip;
) =
DECLARE
   SDCard  = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   Card    = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
ENDDECLARE
BEGIN 
   /*
   **  Only check when SDVIS device is being transferred.
   */
   IF SE.EquipClass <> Type$SDVIS THEN
      RETURN;
   ENDIF;
   /*
   **  Only transfer links for 27kV cards.
   */
   IF C.TypeOfCard = TypeOfCard$4KV THEN
      RETURN;
   ENDIF;
   /*
   **  Find the StepDown card that this equipment is on.
   */
   Card = 0;
   SELECT :SDCard = L.StepDownCard,
          :Card = L.Card
   FROM    Udb_Grouping G,
           SOA_ActiveObject AO,
           FMS_StepDownLink L
   WHERE   G.Member = :SE.Equip AND
           G.Relationship = :Interaction$SourceBreaker AND
           G.Grouping = AO.Object AND
           AO.Card = L.StepDownCard;

   IF Card <> 0 THEN
      CALLPROC FMS_StepDownLinkUpd
          (OldCard = Card,
           Card = C.Card,                   
           OldStepDownCard = SDCard,
           StepDownCard = 0);   /* Triggers update of Card */
      CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
      FCFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'RefreshCardLinks');
   ENDIF;         
          
   RETURN;
END;
				 *Default Item


Name:      helptext

				Fieldobject Script
				------------------

ON CLICK =
BEGIN
    HelpTextObject.FrameName = CurFrame.ObjectSource.Name;
    HelpTextObject.WindowTitle = CurFrame.WindowTitle;
    HelpTextFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'DisplayText');
END;

Application Component Report
============================

	Name:            TransferPhaseCheckEquipment

/*
**      Copyright c 2013 Pateric Software LLC.  All rights reserved.
**
**      Pateric Software proprietary and trade secret information.
**      Do not copy or disclose to third parties without written permission
**      from an officer of Pateric Software LLC. 
**
**  Application:    CAC
**  Frame:          TransferPhaseCheckEquipment 
**
**  History:
**  10/14/13  ysp  Created
**  06/14/17  ysp  Add transfer of phase checks from Known-Point-ISO. Use the 
**                 CardClass field to identify KPS.
**
*/
PROCEDURE TransferPhaseCheckEquipment (
   Equip = INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Equip*/
   EquipName = VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;  /*Passed Equip*/
   OldFeeder 	= INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Source Feeder */
   OldFeederName = VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;  /*Passed Source Feeder */
   NewFeeder 	= INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Destination Feeder */
   NewFeederName = VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;  /*Passed Destination Feeder */
   
   i = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   PhaseCheckEquip = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   SatisfyEquip = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   NewCard = FMS_Card;		 /* destination card */  
   NewJob = JobInProgress;
   NewPermit = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   OldCard = FMS_Card;
   OldPermit = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   RetCode = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Return Code*/
) =
BEGIN
   PhaseCheckEquip = 0;
   SatisfyEquip = 0;

   SELECT :PhaseCheckEquip = P.PhaseCheckEquip,
          :SatisfyEquip = P.SatisfyEquip,
          :OldPermit = P.WorkPermit,
          :OldCard.Card = C.Card,
          :OldCard.TypeOfCard = C.TypeOfCard,
          :OldCard.CardClass = C.CardClass
   FROM   SOA_ActiveObject AO,
          FMS_Card C,
          FMS_PhaseCheck P
   WHERE  AO.Object = :OldFeeder AND
          AO.ObjectToCardLink = 1 AND
          AO.Card = C.Card AND
          AO.Card = P.Card AND
          (P.PhaseCheckEquip = :Equip OR 
          P.SatisfyEquip = :Equip) AND
          P.CompletionTime IS NULL;          
   CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;

   /* not a phase check equipment
   */
   IF PhaseCheckEquip = 0 AND SatisfyEquip = 0 THEN
      RETURN;
   ENDIF;

   IF NewFeeder > 0 AND (OldCard.TypeOfCard = Type$ISOCard OR OldCard.CardClass = Type$ISO) THEN
      SELECT :NewCard.Card = C.Card, 
             :NewCard.TypeOfCard = C.TypeOfCard
      FROM   SOA_ActiveObject AO,
             FMS_Card C
      WHERE  AO.Object = :NewFeeder AND
             AO.ObjectToCardLink = 1 AND
             AO.Card = C.Card;
      
      IF NewCard.Card = 0 THEN
         MESSAGE 'Equipment ' + EquipName + ' is an outstanding phase check on ' + OldFeederName + 
                 '. But there is no active card for ' + NewFeederName + 
                 ' to transfer phase checks to. Phase checks could only be manually transferred.';
         RETURN;
      ENDIF;
         
      /*
      ** create a copy of the work permit on the destination card
      */
      SELECT :NewJob.Job = -1, 
            :NewJob.JobClass = J.JobClass,
            :NewJob.Equip = J.Equip,
            :NewJob.EquipClass = J.EquipClass,  
            :NewJob.MoveEquipClass = SJ.MoveEquipClass,  
            :NewJob.EquipClassName = J.EquipClassName,  
            :NewJob.PrintID = SJ.PrintID,
            :NewJob.EquipName = J.EquipName,
            :NewJob.StepPair = SJ.StepPair,
            :NewJob.MoveType = J.MoveType,
            :NewJob.TOMove = J.TOMove,
            :NewJob.RSMove = J.RSMove,
            :NewJob.TOMoveRules = J.TOMoveRules,
            :NewJob.RSMoveRules = J.RSMoveRules,
            :NewJob.Response = J.Response,
            :NewJob.MoveFGColor = J.MoveFGColor,
            :NewJob.MoveBGColor = J.MoveBGColor,
            :NewJob.ControlCard = J.ControlCard,
            :NewJob.Substation = J.Substation,
            :NewJob.MoveCategory = J.MoveCategory,
            :NewJob.ActivityIdentifier = J.ActivityIdentifier
      FROM   SOA_JobControl SJ,
             SOA_Job J
      WHERE  SJ.Card = :OldCard.Card AND
             SJ.Job = :OldPermit AND
             SJ.Job = J.Job;
      
      NewJob.Card = NewCard.Card;       
      NewJob.Status = 'Hid';   // Hidden
      NewJob.TOOperator = NULL;
      NewJob.TOIssued = '';
      NewJob.TOComplete = '';
      NewJob.RSOperator = NULL;
      NewJob.RSIssued = '';
      NewJob.RSComplete = '';
      NewJob.TOMove = 'ISO ' + OldFeederName + ': ' + NewJob.TOMove;

      NewPermit = NewJob.InsertMove ( 
                  CardTypeOfCard = NewCard.TypeOfCard,
                  KeepMoveText = TRUE);
      NewJob.Job = NewPermit;

      IF NewPermit <= 0 THEN
         CALLPROC TraceError(
               UserMessage = 'Error creating a work permit on the main feeder to transfer phase checks to. ' +
                             'You will have to transfer phase checks manually.',
               TraceMessage = 'Error creating a dummy work permit to transfer phase checks.');
         RETURN;
      ENDIF;  

      /* insert a record in fms_workpermit table so that it can shows up 
      ** on phase check screen 
      */
      RetCode = CALLPROC FMS_WorkPermitUpdate(
                             TOMove = NewJob.TOMove,
                             RSMove = NewJob.RSMove,
                             Description = 'Copied from ISO ' + OldFeederName,
                             Job = NewPermit,
                             EstTimeComplete = '',
                             ProtectionRequired = 0,
                             Warning = 0);
      IF RetCode =  0 THEN
         CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
      ELSE
         CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
         CALLPROC TraceError(
                     UserMessage = 'Error creating a work permit on the main feeder to transfer phase checks to. ' + 
                                   'You will have to set up phase checks manually.',
                     TraceMessage = 'Failed to update dummy work permit to transfer phase checks');
      ENDIF;

      /*
      ** now, transfer all phase checks - primaries and alternates - under the old work permit 
      ** to the new permit. The reason for transferring all is that eventually all equipment will
      ** be transferred from ISO to the main feeder. 
      */                             
      RetCode = CALLPROC FMS_XferPhaseCheckEquip(
                  Equip = PhaseCheckEquip,
                  OldCard = OldCard.Card,
                  OldPermit = OldPermit,
                  NewCard = NewCard.Card,
                  NewPermit = NewPermit);
      IF RetCode =  0 THEN
         CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
      ELSE
         CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
         CALLPROC TraceError(
                     UserMessage = 'Failed to transfer phase check equipment '  + EquipName + ' to new feeder',
                     TraceMessage = 'Failed to transfer the phase check equipment '  + 
                                   EquipName + ' to new feeder = ' + VARCHAR(NewFeederName));
      ENDIF;
   ELSE
      /* Equipment is dropped from the feeder
      */
      IF PhaseCheckEquip = Equip THEN
         /*
         ** delete the whole phase check if it is the primary target
         */
         RetCode = CALLPROC FMS_PhaseCheckDel (
                       Card = OldCard.Card, 
                       WorkPermit = OldPermit, 
                       PhaseCheckEquip = PhaseCheckEquip, 
                       SatisfyEquip = 0);
         IF RetCode =  0 THEN
            CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
         ELSE
            CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
         ENDIF;
         
      ELSEIF SatisfyEquip = Equip THEN
         /*
         ** delete the alternate and leave the primary phase check
         */
         RetCode = CALLPROC FMS_PhaseCheckDel (
                       Card = OldCard.Card, 
                       WorkPermit = OldPermit, 
                       PhaseCheckEquip = PhaseCheckEquip, 
                       SatisfyEquip = SatisfyEquip);
         IF RetCode = 0 THEN
            CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
         ELSE
            CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
         ENDIF;
      ENDIF;
   ENDIF;
END;

Application Component Report
============================

	Name:            TransferShadowItemMoves

/*
**
**      Copyright c 1999 Cegelec ESCA Corporation.  All rights reserved.
**
**      Cegelece ESCA Corporation proprietary and trade secret information.
**      Do not copy or disclose to third parties without written permission
**      from an officer of Cegelec ESCA Corporation.
**
*/
/*
**  Application:    SOA
**  Frame:          TransferShadowItemMoves
**
**  Date:       Author   Description
** ----------------------------------
**  12/13/99	EM       Created
**  09/18/02    ysp      Add GroundOn and MoveFGColor to SOA_TransferEquipJob.
**  03/07/03    em       Corrected run-time syntax error on J.
**  11/12/03    em       Add Job Status "tabled" to transfer job selection.
**
*/
PROCEDURE TransferShadowItemMoves
(
   SourceCard		= INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Card*/
   TargetCard		= INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Card*/
   Equip                = INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Equip*/

   ControlEntry         = NewMoveCard DEFAULT NULL; /*New Control Entry*/
   i			= INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Counter*/
   Moves                = ARRAY OF Job;  /* Existing Equipment moves */
   RetCode              = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Return Code*/
   ShadowItems          = ARRAY OF NewMoveCard;  /*Source card shadow items*/
) =
BEGIN
/*
** Find all moves on the source card that are also in shadow switching items
** for the source card.
*/
   i = 1;
   REPEATED
   SELECT   :Moves[i].Card = JC2.Card,
            :Moves[i].Job = J1.Job,
            :Moves[i].TOIssued = J1.TOIssued,
            :Moves[i].RSIssued = J1.RSIssued,
            :Moves[i].TOComplete = J1.TOComplete,
            :Moves[i].MoveEquipClass = JC1.MoveEquipClass,
            :Moves[i].StepPair = JC3.StepPair,
            :Moves[i].Substation = J1.Substation,
            :Moves[i].PrintID = JC1.PrintID,
            :Moves[i].GroundOn = J1.GroundOn ,
            :Moves[i].MoveFGColor = J1.MoveFGColor 
   FROM     SOA_JobControl JC1,
            SOA_Job J1,
            SOA_JobControl JC2,
            SOA_Job J2,
            SOA_JobControl JC3
   WHERE    JC1.Card = :SourceCard AND
            JC1.Job = J1.Job AND
            J1.Equip = :Equip AND
            J1.MoveCategory = :MoveCategory$Normal AND
            J1.Substation <> 0 AND
            J1.Status IN ('',:JobStatus$NIS,:JobStatus$Table) AND
            J1.Job = JC3.Job AND
            JC3.Card <> JC1.Card AND
            JC3.Card = JC2.Card AND
            JC2.Job <> JC3.Job AND
            JC2.Job = J2.Job AND
            J2.MoveCategory = :MoveCategory$SwitchingItem AND
            J2.ShadowLink = :SourceCard AND
            J2.SwItemStatus = :Card$Active
    BEGIN       
/*
**  Find New ShadowSwitching item for the move on the same
**  card that has the old shadow switching item.
*/              
       SELECT :Moves[i].SwitchingItem = JC4.SwitchingItem
       FROM   SOA_Job J4,
              SOA_JobControl JC4
       WHERE  JC4.Card = :Moves[i].Card AND
              JC4.Job = J4.Job AND
              J4.MoveCategory = :MoveCategory$SwitchingItem AND
              J4.SwItemStatus = :Card$Active AND
              J4.ShadowLink = :TargetCard;

       i = i + 1;
    END;        
/*
**  Mark the move as transferred on the old shadow switching item and insert
**  a control for the new one.
*/
   ControlEntry = NewMoveCard.Create();
   FOR i = 1 TO Moves.LastRow() DO
/*
**  Default specific fields for job insertion.  DB Proc will also copy 
**  existing control entries for this job to the new job, to establish the
**  link for the old switching item for historical purposes.
*/
      IF Moves[i].TOIssued IS NULL THEN
         Moves[i].TOIssued = '';
      ENDIF;
      IF Moves[i].RSIssued IS NULL THEN
         Moves[i].RSIssued = '';
      ENDIF;
      IF Moves[i].TOComplete IS NULL THEN
         Moves[i].TOComplete = '';
      ENDIF;
      IF Moves[i].RSComplete IS NULL THEN
         Moves[i].RSComplete = '';
      ENDIF;
      Moves[i].Status = 'Xfr';
      Moves[i].Response = 'SW Item Xfer';      

      RetCode = CALLPROC SOA_TransferEquipJob (
         Card = Moves[i].Card
        ,Job = Moves[i].Job
        ,TOIssued = Moves[i].TOIssued
        ,TOComplete = Moves[i].TOComplete
        ,RSIssued = Moves[i].RSIssued
        ,RSComplete = Moves[i].RSComplete
        ,Status = Moves[i].Status
        ,Response = Moves[i].Response
        ,GroundOn = Moves[i].GroundOn
        ,MoveFGColor = Moves[i].MoveFGColor
        ); 

      IF RetCode <> 0 THEN
         CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
         MESSAGE 'Procedure:TransferShadowItemMoves;  Unable to mark job ' +
                 'as transferred for old switching item. ' +
                 'Transfer is incomplete - contact Tech Support';
      ELSE
         CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
      ENDIF;
/*      
**  Establish control entries for new switching linking to the original move
*/       
      ControlEntry.Application = Application$SLC;
      ControlEntry.Card = Moves[i].Card;
      ControlEntry.MoveEquipClass = Moves[i].MoveEquipClass;
      ControlEntry.PrintID = Moves[i].PrintID;
      ControlEntry.StepHeading = Moves[i].StepPair;
      ControlEntry.StepLevel = 0;
      ControlEntry.SwitchingItem = Moves[i].SwitchingItem;
      ControlEntry.TypeOfCard = TypeOfCard$SLC; 
         
      Retcode = Moves[i].InsertControl (
                  ControlEntry = ControlEntry
                 ,InitiatingCard = TargetCard
                 ,TransferFlag = TRUE
                 );
      IF RetCode = PU_CANCEL THEN
            MESSAGE 'Procedure:TransferShadowItemMoves; Unable to establish ' +
                    'insert move control for the new switching item.' +
                    'Transfer is incomplete - contact Tech Support';
      ENDIF;          
   ENDFOR;
END;

Application Component Report
============================

	Name:            TransferSWItemEquip

/*
**
**      Copyright c 1998 Cegelec ESCA Corporation.  All rights reserved.
**
**      Cegelece ESCA Corporation proprietary and trade secret information.
**      Do not copy or disclose to third parties without written permission
**      from an officer of Cegelec ESCA Corporation.
**
*/
/*
**  Application:    SOA
**  Frame:          TransferSWItemEquip
**
**  Date:       Author   Description
** ----------------------------------
**  07/13/98	EM       Created
**  08/04/98    pkw      If activating a switching item, we want to make sure
**                       we aren't duplicating moves.
**  09/18/02    ysp      Add GroundOn and MoveFGColor to SOA_TransferEquipJob.
**  11/12/03    em       Add Job Status "tabled" to transfer job selection.
**
*/
PROCEDURE TransferSWItemEquip
(
   Card			= INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Card*/
   Equip                = INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Equip*/
   EventText     	= VARCHAR(256) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   NewSwitchingItem    	= INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Switching Item*/
   OldSwitchingItem 	= INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Switching Item*/
   SWActivating         = INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Flag sometimes*/
   toActive             = INTEGER NOT NULL;  /*Passed Flag sometimes*/

   ControlEntry         = NewMoveCard DEFAULT NULL; /*New Control Entry*/
   i			= INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Counter*/
   Idx                  = ARRAY OF IntegerObject; /*Track impacted cards*/
   ImpactedCardList     = ARRAY OF IntegerObject; /*Track impacted cards*/
   InsertControl        = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Flag*/
   InsertionList        = ARRAY OF NewMoveCard; /*List of cards to insert move*/
   k			= INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Counter*/
   LastRow              = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Counter*/
   Moves                = ARRAY OF Job;  /* Existing Equipment moves */
   n			= INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Counter*/
   NewItemMoves         = ARRAY OF Job;  /* New SwitchingItem Moves */
   RetCode              = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Return Code*/
   TypeOfCard           = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Type of Card */
) =
BEGIN
/*
** Initialize variable
*/
   InsertControl = TRUE;

   SELECT  :TypeOfCard = TypeOfCard
   FROM    SOA_ActiveCard
   WHERE   Card = :Card;
/*
** Selected outstanding moves on equipment
*/
   i = 1;
   Moves.Clear();
   REPEATED 
   SELECT   :Moves[i].Job         = J.Job
           ,:Moves[i].TOIssued    = J.TOIssued
           ,:Moves[i].TOComplete  = J.TOComplete
           ,:Moves[i].RSIssued    = J.RSIssued
           ,:Moves[i].RSComplete  = J.RSComplete
           ,:Moves[i].JobClass    = J.JobClass
           ,:Moves[i].Equip       = J.Equip
           ,:Moves[i].EquipClass  = J.EquipClass
           ,:Moves[i].MoveEquipClass = JC.MoveEquipClass
           ,:Moves[i].PrintID        = JC.PrintID
           ,:Moves[i].StepLevel      = JC.StepLevel
           ,:Moves[i].Substation     = J.Substation
           ,:Moves[i].StepPair       = JC.StepPair
           ,:Moves[i].GroundOn       = J.GroundOn
           ,:Moves[i].MoveFGColor    = J.MoveFGColor
   FROM     SOA_Job J,
            SOA_JobControl JC
   WHERE    J.Equip = :Equip AND
            J.Status IN ('',:JobStatus$NIS,:JobStatus$Table) AND
            (J.TOComplete IS NULL OR J.RSComplete IS NULL) AND
            J.Job = JC.Job AND
         
            JC.Card = :Card AND
            JC.SwitchingItem = :OldSwitchingItem
   BEGIN
      i = i + 1;
   END;
   CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;

   IF SWActivating = TRUE THEN
/*
**  We want to get a list of moves that exist in new switching item
**  so that we don't duplicate a move that shouldn't be.
*/
      i = 1;
      NewItemMoves.Clear();
      REPEATED 
      SELECT   :NewItemMoves[i].Job         = J.Job
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].TOIssued    = J.TOIssued
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].TOComplete  = J.TOComplete
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].RSIssued    = J.RSIssued
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].RSComplete  = J.RSComplete
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].JobClass    = J.JobClass
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].Equip       = J.Equip
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].EquipClass  = J.EquipClass
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].MoveEquipClass = JC.MoveEquipClass
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].PrintID        = JC.PrintID
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].StepLevel      = JC.StepLevel
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].Substation      = J.Substation
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].StepPair       = JC.StepPair
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].GroundOn       = J.GroundOn
              ,:NewItemMoves[i].MoveFGColor    = J.MoveFGColor
      FROM     SOA_Job J,
               SOA_JobControl JC
      WHERE    J.Equip = :Equip AND
               J.Status IN ('',:JobStatus$NIS,:JobStatus$Table) AND
              (J.TOComplete IS NULL OR J.RSComplete IS NULL) AND
               J.Job = JC.Job AND         
               JC.Card = :Card AND
               JC.SwitchingItem = :NewSwitchingItem
      BEGIN
         i = i + 1;
      END;
      CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
   ENDIF;

   ControlEntry = NewMoveCard.Create();

   ImpactedCardList.Clear();
   i = 1;
   LastRow = Moves.LastRow();
   FOR i = 1 TO LastRow DO
/*
**  Default specific fields for job insertion.  DB Proc will also copy 
**  existing control entries for this job to the new job, to establish the
**  link for the old switching item for historical purposes.
*/
      IF Moves[i].TOIssued IS NULL THEN
         Moves[i].TOIssued = '';
      ENDIF;
      IF Moves[i].RSIssued IS NULL THEN
         Moves[i].RSIssued = '';
      ENDIF;
      IF Moves[i].TOComplete IS NULL THEN
         Moves[i].TOComplete = '';
      ENDIF;
      IF Moves[i].RSComplete IS NULL THEN
         Moves[i].RSComplete = '';
      ENDIF;
      Moves[i].Status = 'Xfr';
      Moves[i].Response = 'SW Item Xfer';      

      RetCode = CALLPROC SOA_TransferEquipJob (
         Card = Card
        ,Job = Moves[i].Job
        ,TOIssued = Moves[i].TOIssued
        ,TOComplete = Moves[i].TOComplete
        ,RSIssued = Moves[i].RSIssued
        ,RSComplete = Moves[i].RSComplete
        ,Status = Moves[i].Status
        ,Response = Moves[i].Response
        ,GroundOn = Moves[i].GroundOn
        ,MoveFGColor = Moves[i].MoveFGColor
        ); 

      IF RetCode <> 0 THEN
         CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
         MESSAGE 'Procedure:TransferSWItemEquip;  Unable to copy job for ' +
                 'historical retention purposes. ' +
                 'Transfer is incomplete - contact Tech Support';
         RETURN PU_CANCEL;
      ELSE
         CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
      ENDIF;
       
      IF SWActivating = TRUE THEN
         InsertControl = TRUE;
         k = 1;
         WHILE k <= NewItemMoves.LastRow() DO
            IF NewItemMoves[k].JobClass = Moves[i].JobClass AND
               NewItemMoves[k].Equip = Moves[i].Equip THEN      
               /* Delete move that was on open switching item. */
               IF toActive = TRUE THEN   
                  /* transferring to active switching item */
                  RetCode = CALLPROC SOA_JobDel (Job = Moves[i].Job);
                  IF RetCode < 0 THEN
                     CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                     MESSAGE 'Procedure:TransferSWItemEquip; Unable to ' +
                             'remove duplicate job:(' + varchar(Moves[i].Job) + 
                             ').  Stray move left in SOA_Job and ' +
                             'SOA_JobControl table.';
                     RETURN PU_CANCEL;
                  ENDIF;
                  InsertControl = FALSE;
               ELSE 
            
                  RetCode = CALLPROC SOA_JobDel (Job = NewItemMoves[k].Job);
                  IF RetCode < 0 THEN
                     CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                     MESSAGE 'Procedure:TransferSWItemEquip; Unable to ' +
                             'remove duplicate job:(' +
                              varchar(NewItemMoves[k].Job) + 
                             ').  Stray move left in SOA_Job and ' +
                             'SOA_JobControl table.';
                     RETURN PU_CANCEL;
                  ENDIF;
                  InsertControl = TRUE;
               ENDIF;
               CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
               /* 
               **  Remove this row from array in case there are 
               **  multiple moves with the same jobclass.
               */
               NewItemMoves.RemoveRow (RowNumber = k);
               ENDLOOP;
            ENDIF;
            k = k + 1;
         ENDWHILE;
      ENDIF;

      IF InsertControl = TRUE THEN
/*      
**  Establish control entries for new switching linking to the original move
*/       
         ControlEntry.Application = Application$SLC;
         ControlEntry.Card = Card;
         ControlEntry.MoveEquipClass = Moves[i].MoveEquipClass;
         ControlEntry.PrintID = Moves[i].PrintID;
         ControlEntry.StepHeading = Moves[i].StepPair;
         ControlEntry.StepLevel = Moves[i].StepLevel;
         ControlEntry.SwitchingItem = NewSwitchingItem;
         ControlEntry.TypeOfCard = TypeOfCard; 
         
         Retcode = Moves[i].InsertControl (
                  ControlEntry = ControlEntry
                 ,InitiatingCard = Card
                 ,TransferFlag = TRUE
                 );
         IF RetCode = PU_CANCEL THEN
            MESSAGE 'Procedure:TransferSWItemEquip; Unable to establish ' +
                    'insert move control for the new switching item.' +
                    'Transfer is incomplete - contact Tech Support';
            RETURN PU_CANCEL;
         ENDIF;          
/*
**  If we are transfering from the SW Item being actived, we need to cascade
**  the moves to all other cards.  If the moves are being transfered from an
**  active item they should already be cascaded so nothing is needed.
*/
         IF SWActivating = TRUE AND
            toActive = TRUE THEN
/*
**  Populate other active cards with moves from this switching item.
*/
            Idx.Clear();
            Idx = CALLPROC CascadeMoves (Move = Moves[i],
                                         Card = Card
                                         );

#           include ManageImpactedCards
         ENDIF;   
      ENDIF;   
   ENDFOR;
/*
**  If moves were transferred from another SW Item, to the Switching item
**  being activated we want to cascade all moves originally on the new 
**  switching item.  We can use all the moves in the NewItemMoves array
**  since we already removed duplicate rows above.  
*/
   IF SWActivating = TRUE AND
      toActive = FALSE THEN
      i = 1;
      WHILE i <= NewItemMoves.LastRow() DO
/*      
**  Populate other active cards with moves from this switching item.
*/       
         Idx.Clear();
         Idx = CALLPROC CascadeMoves (Move = NewItemMoves[i],
                                      Card = Card
                                      );   
#        include ManageImpactedCards    
     
         i = i + 1;
      ENDWHILE;
   ENDIF;
      
#  include NotifyImpactedCards

   RETURN PU_OK;
END;

