============================

	Name:            TransferTo

/*
**      Copyright c 1993 ESCA Corporation  All rights reserved.
**
**      ESCA Corporation proprietary and trade secret information.
**      Do not copy or disclose to third parties without written permission
**      from an officer of ESCA Corporation. 
**
**  Application:    CAC
**  Frame:          TransferTo 
**
**  Date:           Version  Description
** --------------------------------------------------
**  JAN 93     adl   author
**  02/08/93   em    JobStatus parm added to callproc
**  02/10/93   em    handled transfer of source equipment.
**  03/09/93   em    renamed TransferTo
**  04/07/93   em    removed repeated select for ddb
**  05/11/93   em    added parameter to transfer job proc call
**  05/26/93   em    added call to originalcard to update feeder
**                   detail.
**  07/30/93   em    log equipment transfer on both cards
**  09/08/93   em    variance fix - set groundon to NULL for xfer job
**  09/30/93   em    reworking transfer to hopefully avoid deadlock
**  10/04/93   em    let user set printid for new feeder
**  11/03/93   em    change sequence of statements following undo.
**  02/16/94   em    look for outto work and active cards on transfer,
**                   related change mad to create iso
**  06/15/94   pw    transfer feeder statuses with equipment
**  04/17/94   mts   Added EquipClass to criteria for select from FMS_JobAction.
**  06/16/94   pw    Add NewEquipMove flag so that screen can be used to
**                   select equipment from iso feeders to add moves to a card
**  06/27/94   hlf   add criteria to select from fms_jobaction
**  07/06/94   mts   Loads TypeOfCard FROM table FMS_Card when doing selects.
**  07/07/94   mts   selections from fms_jobaction now look at equipclass heiarchy.
**  07/11/94   pw    check when Xfer to subfeeder that source equip was chosen
**  09/21/94   pw    confirm source equipment when creating subfeeder
**  10/26/94   hlf   Modify checks/actions to look for moveequipclass  
**  11/15/94   em    Handle passthru of source breaker when creating subfeeder
**  03/23/95   pw    Took out dead moves code that was being repeated
**  05/09/95   pw    Take out code that gets rid of 'N' flag.  This is now done in
**                   database procedure.
**  08/08/95   em    when transferring equipment grouped with macro equipment
**                   (like an ATS), the macro equipment is transferred via
**                   a db rule/procedure.  Moves associated with the macro
**                   equipment will be handled in this procedure using the
**                   transfer jobs procedure.                   
**  08/11/95   em    Watch out for Macro Equip = 0 when transferring moves
**  04/22/96   wc    Added codes to remove any BT statuses
**                        related to this JobClass and equipment
**   12/13/96   em   Call FMS_ManageCardHeader for old and new cards if grounded
**                   equipment has been transferred.
**   03/17/97   jfl  Use MacroGrouper to exclude grouper types.
**   07/24/98   em   Reverse order of Equipment Name and Type.
**   07/25/98   em   Performance; removed NOT IN Grouper sub-select
**   08/26/02   em   OrigCard not diplayed if this is a Popup.  Give a 
**                   confirmationpopup second chance on all Cancel clicks,
**                   not just if an equipment is selected.
**   09/11/02   ysp  Merge: Convert to common job tables.
**   01/22/03   ysp  Set the ActivityIdentifier to 'T' for transferred jobs on the
**                   destination card. 
**   01/22/03   em   Set ActivityIdentifier to 'T' only if not 'S'
**   02/03/03   em   Change text that gets logged; Adjust Dead move count if
**                   necessary
**   02/04/03   ysp  Split the transfer of Feeder Statuses into two steps: Undo and Upd 
**                   steps.  This is because the InsertControl of the Job class will update
**                   the statuses in the new card.
**   05/07/03   pkw  Don't allow equipment that has outstanding FOD moves to be transferred. 
**   05/15/06   ysp  Allow to pass in SelectEquip.
**   06/02/06   ysp  return PU_OK if equipment has been transferred, otherwise, pu_cancel.
**   07/07/06   ysp  itc 184: added checking if the equip has moves in outstanding orders.
**   09/12/06   ysp  Don't allow de-selecting equipment if SelectEquip is passed in.
**   01/12/07   em   On transfer to sub feeder, only show confirm choice if one
**                   device is in substation.
**   03/30/09   em   Added KPS parms to control KPS Source transfer.
**   04/17/09   em   When selecting equip for transfer, check if equip is already on the target
**                   feeder and if the equip is the source breaker for the current feeder (KPS). Use 
**                   "IsAssigned" attribute of FMS_Equip class to record and act:
**                       0 = Not on target feeder, complete transfer normally
**                       1 = Is on target feeder, do not add to target or transfer jobs, but delete
**                           from current feeder
**                       2 = Is KPS Source Breaker, same action as =1 plus update primarygrouping
**                           to target feeder.
**   04/21/09   em  Changed subfeeder label per Mike; Add processing for FCR Return Options from KPS  
**   06/18/09   em  Scroll through passed in equip list and retrieve Print ID 
**   08/13/09   em  Leave Control for KPS_SB moves on the main card.
**   08/23/10   em  Exclude 3G Switch from list; Add ISOFeeder parm for Create ISO
**   12/17/12   em  Exclude ATS Grouper from transfer equipment list.
**   07/24/13   ysp call TransferPhaseCheckEquip after FMS_TransferEquip call is successfully completed
**   08/27/13   em  KPS_SB.Description should be set based on subfeeder type.
**   09/07/13   pkw Pair selects of SD-VIS and SD-TRANSF.
**   11/24/14   pkw call frame when combining KPI and Sectionalized feeders.
**   04/25/15   pkw When creating KPS feeder check for protection links and RFPs
**   04/21/16   ysp 1. For 33kv, load all equipment for all portions on the card. 2. Set Feeder and FeederName
**                  attributes in SelectEquip because equipment are members of different portions. Use SelectEquip.Feeder
**                  instead of FeederObj when processing transfer. 
**   09/14/16   em  Fix bug calling ManageCardHeader for 33kV feeder portion
**   05/08/17   em  Improper handling of 3G ISOFeeder parameter corrected
**   08/17/17   em  If we are handling a KPS transfer, pre-select "downstreamfrom" equipment
**   10/03/17   em  Populate selection list on right for KPS transfer
**   12/27/17   em  Add handling for DownstreamFrom Selection
**   02/21/18   em  Correcting DownstreamFrom selection to use DestinationFeeder.
**                  Always prompt for KPISO if target feeder has an SF6.
**   02/23/18   em  Handle chained downstream SF6 switches.  Limited to two, would need
**                  a more complex solution for more than two chained SF6 switches.
**   03/12/18   em  Improper KPISO prompt when equip already has DSF relationship.
**                  Include PrintID for KPS equipment.
**   09/16/19   em  Prompt to transfer MTA Isolation equipment
**   12/30/19	em	Include DMEaton in DMSF6 type list
**   03/24/20   em   Add call to MarkDiagramInvalid passing both feeders.
*/

INITIALIZE   
(   C = FMS_Card;		          /* parameter - current card */ 
    ISOFeeder = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;  /* parameter */
    ISOFeederName = VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;  /* parameter */
    DestinationFeeder = integer not null; /* parameter - feeder to move equipment to */ 
    Jobs = ARRAY of Job;                  /* parameter - all jobs for current card */ 
    CreateSubFeederFLG = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;  /* parameter */
    EquipSubstation = FMS_Equip;                         /* parameter */
    BreakerEquip = FMS_Equip;                            /* parameter */
    TempSubstation = INTEGER NOT NULL;                   /* parameter */
    KPS_SB = FMS_Equip;                           /* Parameter from CreateKnownPointSplice */
    KPS_SP = FMS_Equip;                           /* Parameter from CreateKnownPointSplice */
    SubFeederType = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;/* Parameter from CreateKnownPointSplice */
    CombineCard = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;/* Parameter from Feedercard combine card menu event */
) = 
DECLARE
    ByPassSelection = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;	
    DC = FMS_Card;		 /* destination card */  
    DownstreamFrom = ARRAY OF INTEGEROBJECT;
    FeederObj = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
    FeederName = VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; 
    SourcePosIndex = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;		 /* index variable */ 
    SourceBkrIndex = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;		 /* index variable */ 
    i = integer not null;	 /* index variable */ 
    j = integer;		 /* index variable */ 
    k = integer not null;
    x = integer;
    ngrounds = integer NOT NULL; /* number of grounds for current equipment */ 
    lastjob = integer not null;		 /* stores index of job of piece of equipment */
    status = integer;        	 /* return status variable */ 
    entrymade = integer;	 /* tests if entry was made */ 
    SelectCount = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
    PrimaryGroupingChange = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
    EquipList = ARRAY OF FMS_Equip; /* List of selected equipment */
    HighLightedEquip = ARRAY of FMS_Equip;
    DynamicWhereClause = VARCHAR(1000) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
    TempSubstationName = VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL;
    OrigCard = FrameExec;
    MacroEquip = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
    EquipGrounded = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;   /* Boolean */
    GroundFeeder = ARRAY OF INTEGEROBJECT;
    DeadMove = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;   /* Boolean */
    ControlEntry = NewMoveCard;
    ControlText = VARCHAR(256) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
    YesFCRWarning = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;   /* Boolean */
    YesDOWarning = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;   /* Boolean */
    DSF = ARRAY OF GroupingClass;
    SF6 = ARRAY OF ObjectClass;

   UpdateSelectedList = PROCEDURE;
   RFP_Link = PROCEDURE;
   SD_Link = PROCEDURE;
   SD_Transfer = PROCEDURE;
   MTA_Check = PROCEDURE;
ENDDECLARE
BEGIN 
   /* Issue message if destination feeder is same as current feeder: */ 
   IF (DestinationFeeder = C.Feeder) THEN 
	   MESSAGE 'Destination feeder is same as current feeder!'; 
	   RETURN PU_CANCEL; 
   /* Issue message if no feeder was selected: */ 
   ELSEIF (DestinationFeeder <= 0) THEN 
	  MESSAGE 'No feeder specified.'; 
	  RETURN PU_CANCEL; 
   ENDIF; 
/*
** Don't display for KPS or combining cards
*/    
   IF KPS_SB.Equip = 0 AND CombineCard = 0 THEN
      OrigCard = OpenFrame OriginalCard (C = C);
   ELSEIF KPS_SB.Equip <> 0 THEN
/*
** Load downstreamfrom equip list.
** Handle a second downstreamfrom chain.
*/
      i = 1;
      j = DSF.LastRow + 1;
      SELECT :DownstreamFrom[i].Value = Member,
             :DSF[j].Member = Member,
             :DSF[j].Grouping = Grouping
      FROM   Udb_Grouping 
      WHERE  Grouping = :KPS_SB.Equip AND
             Relationship = :Interaction$DownstreamFrom
      BEGIN
         i = i + 1;
         j = j + 1;
         SELECT :DownstreamFrom[i].Value = Member,
                :DSF[j].Member = Member,
                :DSF[j].Grouping = Grouping
         FROM   Udb_Grouping 
         WHERE  Grouping = :DownstreamFrom[i-1].Value AND
                Relationship = :Interaction$DownstreamFrom
         BEGIN
            i = i + 1;
            j = j + 1;
         END;
      END;
   ENDIF;
/*
**  Only show selected equip table when creating KPS feeder
*/
   IF SubFeederType <> Type$KPSFeeder THEN
      FIELD(SelectedEquip).ALLBIAS = FB_INVISIBLE;
   ENDIF;

   IF CombineCard = 1 THEN
      FIELD(Transfer_Btn).TextLabel = 'Transfer Equipment and ' + HC_NewLine +
                                      'close ''' + C.FeederName + ''' card';
   ENDIF;
  /* Get the destination card: */ 
   REPEATED
   SELECT :DC.Card = CC.Card, 
          :DC.TypeOfCard = CC.TypeOfCard,
          :DC.SubstationName = CC.SubstationName, 
          :DC.Cutin = CC.Cutin,
          :DC.Cutout = CC.Cutout,
          :DC.Feeder = CC.Feeder,                               
          :DC.Status = CC.Status, 
          :DC.GroundsOn = CC.GroundsOn, 
          :DC.FeederName = CC.FeederName, 
          :DestinationFeederName = CC.FeederName  
   FROM   FMS_Card CC,
          SOA_ActiveObject AO 
   WHERE  AO.Object = :DestinationFeeder AND  
          AO.ObjectToCardLink = 1 AND
          AO.Card = CC.Card; 
          
   IF DC.TypeOfCard = TypeOfCard$Portion THEN      // 33KV Portion 
      SELECT :DestinationFeederName = O.Name
      FROM   UDB_Grouping G,
             UDB_Object O
      WHERE  G.Member = :DestinationFeeder AND
             G.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
             G.GroupingType = :Type$Feeder AND
             G.Grouping = O.Object;
   ENDIF;
   CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;

   IF DC.Card = 0 THEN
      Message 'Unable to find card to which moves are to be ' +
              'transferred';
      RETURN PU_CANCEL;
   ENDIF;

   IF C.NetworkFeeder = NetworkFeeder$3G THEN
      IF ISOFeeder > 0 THEN
         FeederObj = ISOFeeder;
         FeederName = ISOFeederName;
         OriginalFeederName = ISOFeederName;   
      ELSE
         FeederObj = C.Object[1].Object;
         FeederName = C.Object[1].Name;

         IF C.Object.LastRow() > 1 THEN
            FIELD(NetworkFeeder).ValueList.ChoiceItems.Clear();
            FOR i = 1 TO C.Object.LastRow() DO
               FIELD(NetworkFeeder).ValueList.ChoiceItems[i].EnumValue = C.Object[i].Object;
               FIELD(NetworkFeeder).ValueList.ChoiceItems[i].EnumText = C.Object[i].Name;
            ENDFOR;
            FIELD(NetworkFeeder).CurBias = FB_CHANGEABLE;
            /* OR5.1 FIELD(NetworkFeeder).ColumnWidthCompressed = TRUE; */
            FIELD(NetworkFeeder).UpdChoiceList();
         ENDIF;
         NetworkFeeder = C.Object[1].Object;
         OriginalFeederName = C.Object[1].Name;      
      ENDIF;  /*ISOFeeder*/
   ELSE
      FeederObj = C.Feeder;
      FeederName = C.FeederName;
      OriginalFeederName = C.FeederName;
      
      // set SB and SP grouping so we can put them back on the original feeder
      KPS_SB.Feeder = FeederObj;
      KPS_SP.Feeder = FeederObj;
   ENDIF;

   entrymade = 0; 
   ByPassSelection = 0;

   IF SelectEquip.LastRow = 0 THEN
      CurFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'load_equip');
   ELSE
      ByPassSelection = 1;
      FOR i = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow() DO
         FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Origin).IsReverse = TRUE;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Description).IsReverse = TRUE;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[i].PrintID).IsReverse = TRUE;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipName).IsReverse = TRUE;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName).IsReverse = TRUE;
/*
** Check for DownstreamFrom
*/                       
          j = DSF.LastRow;             
          j = j + 1;
          SELECT :DSF[j].Member = Member,
                 :DSF[j].Grouping = Grouping
          FROM   Udb_Grouping
          WHERE  Member = :SelectEquip[i].Equip AND
                 Relationship = :Interaction$DownstreamFrom;
         
         /* For 3G or 33kv, get the portion/feeder where the equipment is a member of.
         ** We will later use SelectEquip[].Feeder to know from which portion/feeder to transfer equiment.
         */
         IF C.NetworkFeeder > 0 THEN 
            SELECT :SelectEquip[i].Feeder = G.Grouping,
                   :SelectEquip[i].FeederName = O.Name
            FROM   UDB_Grouping G,
                   UDB_Object O
            WHERE G.Member = :SelectEquip[i].Equip AND
                  G.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                  G.GroupingType IN (SELECT Type 
                                     FROM   UDB_ExtendedType
                                     WHERE  SuperType = :Type$Feeder) AND
                  G.Grouping = O.Object;
         ELSE
            SelectEquip[i].Feeder = C.Feeder;
            SelectEquip[i].FeederName = C.FeederName;
         ENDIF;
         
         SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID = SelectEquip[i].PrintID;
         IF SelectEquip[i].PrintID = '' THEN  /* Confirm PrintID for all cases */
            SELECT :SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID = Reference,
                   :SelectEquip[i].PrintID = Reference
            FROM   Udb_Grouping
            WHERE  Grouping = :SelectEquip[i].Feeder AND
                   Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                   Member = :SelectEquip[i].Equip;
         ENDIF;  
      ENDFOR;
   ENDIF;
END;

ON SETVALUE NetWorkFeeder =
BEGIN
      FeederObj = FIELD(NetworkFeeder).CurEnumValue;
      FeederName = FIELD(NetworkFeeder).CurEnumText;
      OriginalFeederName = FIELD(NetworkFeeder).CurEnumText;

      IF (DestinationFeeder = FeederObj) THEN 
	   MESSAGE 'Destination feeder is same as current feeder!'; 
	   RETURN PU_CANCEL; 
      ENDIF; 
      CurFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'load_equip');
END;

ON UserEvent 'load_equip' =
DECLARE
   LastRow = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   RowFound = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
BEGIN
   SelectEquip.Clear();	/* Clear out storage */ 
   i = 1;
   
   IF C.NetworkFeeder = NetworkFeeder$33KV THEN
      /* Load equipment list for portions on current feeder: */
      REPEATED
      SELECT :SelectEquip[i].Equip = O.Object, 
             :SelectEquip[i].EquipName = O.Name, 
             :SelectEquip[i].EquipClass  = O.Type,
             :SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName  = O.TypeName,
             :SelectEquip[i].PrintID = G.Reference, 
             :SelectEquip[i].Origin = O.OwnerNumber, 
             :SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID = G.Reference, 
             :SelectEquip[i].Description = O.Description,
             :SelectEquip[i].IsAssigned = 0,
             :SelectEquip[i].Feeder = G.Grouping            // original portion feeder 
       FROM   TFMS_CardToObject CTO,
              Udb_Object O, 
              Udb_Grouping G 
       WHERE  CTO.Card = :C.Card AND
              CTO.Object = G.Grouping AND 
              G.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
              G.Member = O.Object AND 
              O.Type IN (SELECT Type
                        FROM   Udb_ExtendedType
                        WHERE  SuperType = :Type$Switch) AND
              O.Type NOT IN (SELECT Type
                               FROM   Udb_ExtendedType
                               WHERE  SuperType IN (:Type$Grouper,:Type$3GSwitch))  
      ORDER BY PrintID, EquipName, Equip
      BEGIN
         SelectEquip[i].FeederName = OriginalFeederName;
         i = i + 1;
      END; 
      
      /* remove duplicate interrupter switches because they are members of two portions.
      */
      i = SelectEquip.LastRow;
      WHILE i >=2 DO
         IF SelectEquip[i-1].Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip THEN
            SelectEquip.RemoveRow(RowNumber = i);
         ENDIF;
         i = i - 1;
      ENDWHILE;
   ELSE
      /* Load equipment list for current feeder: */
      REPEATED
      SELECT :SelectEquip[i].Equip = O.Object, 
             :SelectEquip[i].EquipName = O.Name, 
             :SelectEquip[i].EquipClass  = O.Type,
             :SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName  = O.TypeName,
             :SelectEquip[i].PrintID = G.Reference, 
             :SelectEquip[i].Origin = O.OwnerNumber, 
             :SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID = G.Reference, 
             :SelectEquip[i].Description = O.Description,
             :SelectEquip[i].IsAssigned = 0,
             :SelectEquip[i].Feeder = G.Grouping       
       FROM   Udb_Object O, 
              Udb_Grouping G 
       WHERE  G.Grouping = :FeederObj AND 
              G.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
              G.Member = O.Object AND 
              G.Member NOT IN (:KPS_SB.Equip, :KPS_SP.Equip) AND
              O.Type IN (SELECT Type
                        FROM   Udb_ExtendedType
                        WHERE  SuperType = :Type$Switch) AND
              O.Type NOT IN (SELECT Type
                               FROM   Udb_ExtendedType
                               WHERE  SuperType IN (:Type$Grouper,:Type$3GSwitch))  
      ORDER BY PrintID, EquipName
      BEGIN
         SelectEquip[i].FeederName = OriginalFeederName;
         i = i + 1;
      END; 
   ENDIF;
   CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
/*
** Pre-select downstreamfrom equip
*/
   IF DownstreamFrom.LastRow > 0 THEN
      LastRow = SelectEquip.LastRow;
      FOR i = 1 TO LastRow DO

         RowFound = DownstreamFrom.Find(AttributeName = 'Value',
                                    Value = SelectEquip[i].Equip);
         IF RowFound = ER_OK THEN
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Origin).IsReverse = TRUE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Description).IsReverse = TRUE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].PrintID).IsReverse = TRUE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipName).IsReverse = TRUE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName).IsReverse = TRUE;
         ENDIF;
      ENDFOR;
      CALLPROC UpdateSelectedList();
   ENDIF;
END; 

/* 
**  Handle an equipment selection from the list:  
*/ 
ON ChildEntry SelectEquip[*].Origin,
ON ChildEntry SelectEquip[*].Description,
ON ChildEntry SelectEquip[*].PrintID,
ON ChildEntry SelectEquip[*].EquipName,
ON ChildEntry SelectEquip[*].EquipClassName = 
BEGIN 
   IF (CurFrame.ReasonCode <> RC_MOUSECLICK) THEN
       RESUME;
   ENDIF;
/*
** if SelectEquip is passed in, don't allow de-selection of equipment.
*/
   IF ByPassSelection = 1 THEN
       RESUME;
   ENDIF;

   EntryMade = 1; 
   IF (FIELD(SelectEquip[].Description).IsReverse = FALSE) THEN
      /*
      ** Check if equip has a move that was downloaded to an Operating Order or FOD Order
      */
      status = CALLPROC CheckOutstandingEquip(Equip = SelectEquip[].Equip);

      IF status = PU_CANCEL THEN
         MESSAGE 'Equipment ' +
            SelectEquip[].EquipClassName + '  ' +
            SelectEquip[].EquipName +
           ' has a move or moves that were downloaded to an order. ' + 
           ' This equipment cannot be transferred ' +
           'until the order processing is complete and confirmed.';
         RESUME;
      ENDIF;

      SELECT :SelectEquip[].IsAssigned = 1
      FROM   Udb_Grouping 
      WHERE  Member = :SelectEquip[].Equip AND
             Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
             Grouping = :DestinationFeeder;

      IF SelectEquip[].IsAssigned = 1 THEN
         SELECT :SelectEquip[].IsAssigned = 2
         FROM   Udb_Grouping 
         WHERE  Member = :SelectEquip[].Equip AND
                Relationship = :Interaction$SourceBreaker AND
                Grouping = :SelectEquip[].Feeder;
      ENDIF;

      FIELD(SelectEquip[].Origin).IsReverse = TRUE;
      FIELD(SelectEquip[].Description).IsReverse = TRUE;
      FIELD(SelectEquip[].PrintID).IsReverse = TRUE;
      FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipName).IsReverse = TRUE;
      FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipClassName).IsReverse = TRUE;

      CALLPROC SD_Link(Object = SelectEquip[].Equip,
                       IsReverse = TRUE,
                       Type = SelectEquip[].EquipClass);

      /*
      **  When creating KPSFeeder, check if equip has moves used for 
      **  work permit protection and rfp link.  
      */
      IF SubFeederType = Type$KPSFeeder THEN
         CALLPROC RFP_Link(Object = SelectEquip[].Equip,
                          IsReverse = TRUE,
                          Card = C.Card);
      ENDIF;
/*
** Check for DownstreamFrom
*/                       
          i = DSF.LastRow;             
          i = i + 1;
          SELECT :DSF[i].Member = Member,
                 :DSF[i].Grouping = Grouping
          FROM   Udb_Grouping
          WHERE  Member = :SelectEquip[].Equip AND
                 Relationship = :Interaction$DownstreamFrom;
   ELSE
      FIELD(SelectEquip[].Origin).IsReverse = FALSE;
      FIELD(SelectEquip[].Description).IsReverse = FALSE;
      FIELD(SelectEquip[].PrintID).IsReverse = FALSE;
      FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipName).IsReverse = FALSE;
      FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipClassName).IsReverse = FALSE;

      CALLPROC SD_Link(Object = SelectEquip[].Equip,
                       IsReverse = FALSE,
                       Type = SelectEquip[].EquipClass);
      /*
      **  When creating KPSFeeder, check if equip has moves used for 
      **  work permit protection and rfp link.  
      */
      IF SubFeederType = Type$KPSFeeder THEN
         CALLPROC RFP_Link(Object = SelectEquip[].Equip,
                          IsReverse = FALSE,
                          Card = C.Card,
                          LinkID = IFNULL(SelectEquip[].G,0));
      ENDIF;
/*
** Remove from DownstreamFrom if it is there
*/                       
          i = DSF.LastRow;
          WHILE i > 0 DO
            IF DSF[i].Member = SelectEquip[].Equip  THEN
               DSF.RemoveRow (RowNumber = i );
               ENDLOOP;
            ENDIF;
            i = i - 1;
          ENDWHILE;
   ENDIF; 
   RESUME; 
END; 

ON Click Cancel_Btn,
ON Click Transfer_Btn =
BEGIN
/*
**  Check to see whether or not the original card data needs to be saved.
*/
    IF (Curframe.TriggerField = FIELD(Transfer_Btn)) THEN
        CALLPROC MTA_Check ();
        OrigCard.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'UpdateCard');
        Curframe.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'ContinueTransfer_Btn');
    ELSE
        OrigCard.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'ExitFrame');
        Curframe.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'ContinueCancel_Btn');
    ENDIF;
END;

/* 
**  Handle a TRANSFER click:  
*/ 
ON UserEvent 'ContinueTransfer_Btn' = 
DECLARE

ENDDECLARE 
BEGIN 
   IF CreateSubFeederFLG = TRUE THEN
      IF KPS_SB.Equip = 0 THEN  /* Source already selected for KPS */
         i = 1;
         j = 1;
         WHILE i <= SelectEquip.LastRow() DO
            IF (FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Description).IsReverse = TRUE) THEN
               HighLightedEquip[j] = SelectEquip[i].Duplicate();
               HighLightedEquip[j].PrintID = SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID;
               j = j + 1;                    
            ENDIF;
            i = i + 1;
         ENDWHILE;
         DynamicWhereClause = 'G.GroupingType IN ( ' + VARCHAR(:Type$Substation) + ',' + 
                  VARCHAR(:Type$UnitSubStation) + ') AND ' +
                 'G.Relationship = ' + varchar(:Interaction$MemberOf) + ' AND ' +
                 'G.Member = O.Object AND G.Grouping = O1.Object AND ' +
                 'G.Member IN ( ';
         i = 1;
         WHILE i <= HighLightedEquip.LastRow() DO
            IF i = HighLightedEquip.LastRow() THEN
               DynamicWhereClause = DynamicWhereClause + 
                     VARCHAR(HighLightedEquip[i].Equip) + ')';
            ELSE
               DynamicWhereClause = DynamicWhereClause + 
                     VARCHAR(HighLightedEquip[i].Equip) + ',';
            ENDIF;
            i = i + 1;
         ENDWHILE;
         
         i = 1;
         SELECT  :EquipList[i].Substation = O1.Object,
                 :EquipList[i].Equip = O.Object, 
                 :EquipList[i].EquipName = O.Name, 
                 :EquipList[i].EquipClass  = O.Type,
                 :EquipList[i].EquipClassName  = O.TypeName,
                 :EquipList[i].PrintID = G.Reference, 
                 :EquipList[i].NewPrintID = G.Reference, 
                 :EquipList[i].Description = O1.Description
         FROM    Udb_Grouping G,
                 Udb_Object O,
                 Udb_Object O1
         WHERE  :DynamicWhereClause
         BEGIN
            i = i + 1;
         END; 
         CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;

         status = PU_CANCEL; 
         IF EquipList.LastRow() = 1 THEN
            status = CALLFRAME ConfirmChoice(EquipName = EquipList[1].EquipName);
         ENDIF;

         IF status = PU_OK THEN
            EquipSubstation = EquipList[1].Duplicate();
            BreakerEquip = EquipList[1].Duplicate();
         ELSE 
            CALLFRAME ChangePrimarySource (CreateSubfeederFLG = TRUE,
                             SelectEquip = HighLightedEquip.Duplicate(),
                             SourceBreakerEquip = byref(SourceBkrIndex),
                             SourcePositionEquip = byref(SourcePosIndex));
            IF SourcePosIndex = 0 THEN
               RETURN PU_OK;
            ELSE
               EquipSubstation = HighLightedEquip[SourcePosIndex].Duplicate(); 
               IF SourceBkrIndex = 0 THEN
                    BreakerEquip = HighLightedEquip[SourcePosIndex].Duplicate(); 
               ELSE
                    BreakerEquip = HighLightedEquip[SourceBkrIndex].Duplicate(); 
               ENDIF;
               /*
               **  See if they selected a piece of equipment that is defined
               **    as source.  If it's not more work to do.
               */
               SELECT  :BreakerEquip.Substation = O1.Object,
                       :BreakerEquip.Description = O1.Description 
               FROM    Udb_Grouping G,
                       Udb_Object O1
               WHERE   G.GroupingType IN (:Type$Substation,:Type$UnitSubStation) AND
                       G.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                       G.Grouping = O1.Object AND
                       G.Member = :BreakerEquip.Equip;

               IF IIRowCount = 0 THEN
                  SELECT :BreakerEquip.Substation = IFNULL(Object,0),
                         :BreakerEquip.Description = 'Subfeeder'
                  FROM   UDB_OBJECT O
                  WHERE  O.Object = (SELECT  MIN(Object)
                                     FROM    UDB_OBJECT D
                                     WHERE   D.Type = :Type$TempSubstation and
                                             varchar(D.Object) = D.Name);
                  CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                  IF BreakerEquip.Substation = 0 THEN
                     Message 'Can not create temporary substation.  The temporary substation ' +
                             'pool is full.  Please contact technical support.';
                     RESUME;
                  ENDIF;
                  /*
                  **  Update object table now so that if someone else is creating a subfeeder
                  **    with a alternate source they will not get same object from the
                  **    temporary substation pool.
                  */
                  TempSubstation = 0;
                  TempSubstation = BreakerEquip.Substation;
                  TempSubstationName = varchar(TempSubstation) + '-TempSubstation';
                  status = CALLPROC FMS_ReturnObject (
                              Object  = BreakerEquip.Substation,
                              Description = BreakerEquip.Description,
                              Name    = TempSubstationName,
                              Type    = Type$TempSubstation,
                              PrimaryGrouping = Unused$TempSubstation);
                  IF status < 0 THEN
                     CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                     Message 'Unable to Create Temporary Substation.';
                     RESUME;
                  ENDIF;
                  CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT; 
               ENDIF;
            ENDIF;
         ENDIF;

      ELSE  /* Just for KPS */
         SELECT  :KPS_SB.Substation = O1.Object,
                 :KPS_SB.Description = O1.Description 
         FROM    Udb_Grouping G,
                 Udb_Object O1
         WHERE   G.GroupingType IN (:Type$Substation,:Type$UnitSubStation) AND
                 G.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                 G.Grouping = O1.Object AND
                 G.Member = :KPS_SB.Equip;

         IF IIRowCount = 0 THEN
            IF SubFeederType = Type$KPSFeeder THEN
               KPS_SB.Description = 'Known Pt ISO Feeder';
            ELSE 
               KPS_SB.Description = 'Sectionalized Feeder';
            ENDIF;
            SELECT :KPS_SB.Substation = IFNULL(Object,0)
            FROM   UDB_OBJECT O
            WHERE  O.Object = (SELECT  MIN(Object)
                               FROM    UDB_OBJECT D
                               WHERE   D.Type = :Type$TempSubstation and
                                       varchar(D.Object) = D.Name);
            IF KPS_SB.Substation = 0 THEN
               Message 'Can not create temporary substation.  The temporary substation ' +
                       'pool is full.  Please contact technical support.';
               RESUME;
            ENDIF;
            /*
            **  Update object table now so that if someone else is creating a subfeeder
            **    with a alternate source they will not get same object from the
            **    temporary substation pool.
            */
            TempSubstation = 0;
            TempSubstation = KPS_SB.Substation;
            TempSubstationName = varchar(TempSubstation) + '-TempSubstation';
            status = CALLPROC FMS_ReturnObject (
                        Object  = KPS_SB.Substation,
                        Description = KPS_SB.Description,
                        Name    = TempSubstationName,
                        Type    = Type$TempSubstation,
                        PrimaryGrouping = Unused$TempSubstation);
            IF status < 0 THEN
               CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
               Message 'Unable to Create Temporary Substation.';
               RESUME;
            ENDIF;
            CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT; 
         ENDIF;
      ENDIF;
   ENDIF;
/*
** Add KPS equip to Select Equip list if not already there as it would be in FCR Return Options.
*/
   IF KPS_SB.Equip <> 0 THEN
      i = 1;
      WHILE i <= SelectEquip.LastRow() DO
         IF SelectEquip[i].Equip = KPS_SB.Equip THEN
            ENDLOOP;
         ENDIF;
         i = i + 1;
      ENDWHILE;
      IF i > SelectEquip.LastRow() THEN
         SelectEquip.InsertRow (RowNumber = 1, RowObject = KPS_SB);
         SelectEquip[1].NewPrintID = KPS_SB.PrintID;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[1].Description).IsReverse = TRUE;
      ENDIF; 
   ENDIF;   
   IF KPS_SP.Equip <> 0 AND KPS_SP.Equip <> KPS_SB.Equip THEN
      i = 1;
      WHILE i <= SelectEquip.LastRow() DO
         IF SelectEquip[i].Equip = KPS_SP.Equip THEN
            ENDLOOP;
         ENDIF;
         i = i + 1;
      ENDWHILE;
      IF i > SelectEquip.LastRow() THEN
         SelectEquip.InsertRow (RowNumber = 1, RowObject = KPS_SP);
        SelectEquip[1].NewPrintID = KPS_SP.PrintID;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[1].Description).IsReverse = TRUE;
      ENDIF; 
   ENDIF;
   
   EquipGrounded = FALSE;   
   DeadMove = FALSE;   
   i = 1;
   WHILE (i <= SelectEquip.LastRow()) DO 

      IF (FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Description).IsReverse = TRUE) THEN

         entrymade = 2; 

         /* Get number of grounds for current piece of equipment: */ 
         ngrounds = 0; 
         SELECT :ngrounds = O.StatusCount
         FROM   FMS_ObjectStatus O 
         WHERE  O.Object = :SelectEquip[i].Equip AND 
                O.Status = :Status$Ground; 
         CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
         IF ngrounds > 0 THEN
            EquipGrounded = TRUE;
            k = GroundFeeder.Find(AttributeName = 'Value',
                                  Value = SelectEquip[i].Feeder);
            IF k = ER_ROWNOTFOUND THEN
               GroundFeeder.InsertRow (RowNumber = 1);
               GroundFeeder[1].Value = SelectEquip[i].Feeder;
            ENDIF; 
         ENDIF;

         /* Is the current Feeder the PrimaryGrouping for the Equipment? */
         PrimaryGroupingChange = 0;
         SELECT :PrimaryGroupingChange = COUNT(*)
         FROM   Udb_Object
         WHERE  Object = :SelectEquip[i].Equip AND
              (PrimaryGrouping = :SelectEquip[i].Feeder OR
               PrimaryGrouping IN (SELECT Object
                                   FROM   Udb_Object
                                   WHERE  Type = :Type$TempSubstation));
         CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;

         IF SelectEquip[i].Equip <> KPS_SB.Equip THEN
            /* drop feeder statuses from the source feeder */
            status = CALLPROC FeederStatusUndo(Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                                          SourceCard = C,
                                          J = Jobs,
                                          Action = 'Xfer');
            IF (status = PU_CANCEL) THEN 
               CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
               MESSAGE 'Unable to drop feeder statuses from current card';
               ENDLOOP;
               RESUME; 
            ENDIF;
            CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
         ENDIF;
           
         IF SelectEquip[i].IsAssigned >= 1 THEN  /* Just delete from current feeder*/

            status = Udb_GroupingDel (Grouping = SelectEquip[i].Feeder,
                                     Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf,
                                     Member = SelectEquip[i].Equip);
            IF status > 0 THEN
               CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
               Message 'Unable to remove ' +
                  SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                  SelectEquip[i].EquipName + ' from current feeder.';
                  
            ELSEIF SelectEquip[i].IsAssigned >= 2 THEN  /* Reset primary grouping to target feeder */
               status = CALLPROC Udb_ObjectUpd (
                                       Object = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                                       PrimaryGrouping = DestinationFeeder,
                                       Type = SelectEquip[i].EquipClass,
                                       Name = SelectEquip[i].EquipName);
               IF status < 0 THEN
                  CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                  Message 'Unable to primary group ' +
                     SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                     SelectEquip[i].EquipName + ' to destination feeder.';
               ENDIF;
            ENDIF;
            CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;

         ELSE
            /* Transfer equip and grounds to the new Feeder */ 
            status = CALLPROC FMS_TransferEquip  
                  (Feeder      = SelectEquip[i].Feeder,  
                   DestFeeder  = DestinationFeeder, 
                   Equip       = SelectEquip[i].Equip, 
                   NewPrintID  = SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID, 
                   MemberOfRelation  = Interaction$MemberOf, 
                   SourcePosRelation = Interaction$SourcePosition,
                   EquipGrounds = ngrounds,
                   GroundStatus = Status$Ground,
                   NewPrimaryGrouping = PrimaryGroupingChange);
    
            IF status <> 0 THEN
               CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
               Message 'Transfer of ' + SelectEquip[i].PrintID + '  ' +
                     SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                     SelectEquip[i].EquipName + ' failed.';

               /* Transfer feeder statuses to back to old feeder */
               status = CALLPROC FeederStatusUpd(Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                                               DestCard = C,
                                               J = Jobs,
                                               Action = 'Xfer');
               IF (status = PU_CANCEL) THEN 
                  CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                  MESSAGE 'Unable to reverse feeder status transfer after equipment ' +
                        'transfer failed.  Feeder Statuses has been transferred, ' +
                        'but the equipment has not.  Contact FMS technical ' +
                        'support.';
                  ENDLOOP;
                  RESUME; 
               ENDIF;
               CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;

               CurFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'load_equip');
               ENDLOOP;
            ELSE
               CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
  
               CALLPROC TransferPhaseCheckEquipment (
                   Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                   EquipName = SelectEquip[i].EquipName,
                   OldFeeder 	= SelectEquip[i].Feeder,
                   OldFeederName = OriginalFeederName,  
                   NewFeeder 	= DestinationFeeder,
                   NewFeederName = DestinationFeederName);
            ENDIF;		      
            
/*
** Put KPS_SB back on original feeder
*/
            IF KPS_SB.Equip <> 0 THEN
               status = CALLPROC Udb_GroupingIns (
                                SystemVersion = 0,
                                Grouping = KPS_SB.Feeder,
                                GroupingType = Type$Feeder,
                                Member = KPS_SB.Equip,
                                MemberType = KPS_SB.EquipClass,
                                Reference = KPS_SB.PrintID,
                                Relationship = Interaction$MemberOf);
               IF status < 0 THEN 
                 CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                 Message 'The KPS Source Breaker lost its common connection to the main feeder.';
               ENDIF;
               CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
            ENDIF;                     
        
            IF CreateSubFeederFLG = TRUE THEN
               IF SelectEquip[i].Equip = BreakerEquip.Equip THEN
               /*
               **  Give source equip primarygrouping of substation again
               */
                  status = CALLPROC Udb_ObjectUpd (
                                          Object = BreakerEquip.Equip,
                                          PrimaryGrouping = BreakerEquip.Substation,
                                          Type = BreakerEquip.EquipClass,
                                          Name = BreakerEquip.EquipName);
                  IF status < 0 THEN
                     CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                     RESUME;
                  ENDIF;
                  CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
               ENDIF;
               IF SelectEquip[i].Equip = KPS_SB.Equip THEN
               /*
               **  Give source equip primarygrouping of substation again
               */
                  status = CALLPROC Udb_ObjectUpd (
                                          Object = KPS_SB.Equip,
                                          PrimaryGrouping = KPS_SB.Substation,
                                          Type = KPS_SB.EquipClass,
                                          Name = KPS_SB.EquipName);
                  IF status < 0 THEN
                     CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                     RESUME;
                  ENDIF;
                  CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
               ENDIF;
            ENDIF;

/*
**   Check if equipment is attached to a macro equipment.  If it is, we will
**   have to transfer moves for that equip as well.
*/
            MacroEquip = 0;
            REPEATED 
            SELECT :MacroEquip = G.Grouping
            FROM   Udb_Grouping G,
                   Udb_ExtendedType ET
            WHERE  G.GroupingType    = ET.Type AND
                   ET.SuperType    = :Type$Switch AND
                   G.Relationship  = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                   G.Member        = :SelectEquip[i].Equip; 
/*
** transfer jobs from the current card to the destination card
*/
            j = 1; 
            WHILE j <= Jobs.LastRow()  DO 

               IF (Jobs[j].Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip OR
                    (Jobs[j].Equip = MacroEquip AND MacroEquip > 0)) AND 
                    Jobs[j].Status = '' THEN

                  IF ((Jobs[j].TOIssued IS NULL) OR   
                       (Jobs[j].TOComplete IS NULL) OR   
                       (Jobs[j].RSIssued   IS NULL) OR   
                       (Jobs[j].RSComplete IS NULL)   ) THEN  

                      /* Blank out any NULL times: */
                     IF (Jobs[j].TOIssued IS NULL) THEN 
                        Jobs[j].ToIssued = ' '; 
                     ENDIF; 
                     IF (Jobs[j].TOComplete IS NULL) THEN 
                       Jobs[j].TOComplete = ' '; 
                     ENDIF; 
                     IF (Jobs[j].RSIssued IS NULL) THEN 
                       Jobs[j].RSIssued = ' '; 
                     ENDIF; 
                     IF (Jobs[j].RSComplete IS NULL) THEN  
                       Jobs[j].RSComplete = ' '; 
                     ENDIF; 

                     IF Jobs[j].MoveType = 'Dead' AND DeadMove = FALSE THEN
                        DeadMove = TRUE;
                     ENDIF;
/*
** Don't transfer KPS_SB
*/
                     IF SelectEquip[i].Equip <> KPS_SB.Equip THEN

                        Jobs[j].Response = 'Xfer to ' + DC.FeederName; 
                        Jobs[j].Status = Job$Xfer; 
                        Jobs[j].GroundOn = NULL;
                        Jobs[j].MoveFGColor = CC_BLACK;

                        /* Update the job on current card: make a copy of the job for 
                        the source card and tranfer the original job to the destination
                        card. */ 
                        status = CALLPROC SOA_TransferEquipJob
                                    ( Card       = C.Card,
                                    Job        = Jobs[j].Job, 
                                    Response   = Jobs[j].Response, 
                                    Status     = Jobs[j].Status, 
                                    TOIssued   = Jobs[j].TOIssued, 
                                    TOComplete = Jobs[j].TOComplete, 
                                    RSIssued   = Jobs[j].RSIssued, 
                                    RSComplete = Jobs[j].RSComplete,
                                    GroundOn   = Jobs[j].GroundOn,
                                    MoveFGColor= Jobs[j].MoveFGColor
                                    ); 
                        IF (status <> 0) THEN 
                           CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                           Message 'Unable to transfer moves related to ' + 
                               SelectEquip[i].PrintID + '  ' +
                               SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                               SelectEquip[i].EquipName + 
                               ' . Equipment transfer failed.';

                           status = CALLPROC FMS_UndoTransferEquip  
                                      (SourceFeeder      = SelectEquip[i].Feeder,  
                                       Feeder  = DestinationFeeder, 
                                       Equip       = SelectEquip[i].Equip, 
                                       OldPrintID  = SelectEquip[i].PrintID, 
                                       MemberOfRelation  = Interaction$MemberOf, 
                                       SourcePosRelation = Interaction$SourcePosition,
                                       EquipGrounds = ngrounds,
                                       GroundStatus = Status$Ground);

                           IF status <> 0 THEN
                              CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                              Message 'Unable to reverse equipment transfer after move ' +
                                'transfer failed.  Equipment has been transferred, ' +
                                'but their moves have not.  Contact FMS technical ' +
                                'support.';
                              ENDLOOP;
                              RESUME; 
                           ENDIF; 
                           CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;

                           status = CALLPROC FeederStatusUpd(Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                                             DestCard = C,
                                             J = Jobs,
                                             Action = 'Xfer');
                           IF (status = PU_CANCEL) THEN 
                            CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                            MESSAGE 'Unable to reverse feeder status transfer after move ' +
                                 'transfer failed.  Feeder Statuses have been dropped from ' +
                                 'the current card. Equipment and moves have not been transferred. ' +
                                 ' Contact FMS technical support.';
                            ENDLOOP;
                            RESUME; 
                           ENDIF;
                           CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;


                           CurFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'load_equip');
                           ENDLOOP;
                        ENDIF;
                        CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
                     ENDIF;
                     /*      
                     **  Establish control entry for destination card linking to the original move
                     */       
                     ControlEntry.Card = DC.Card;
                     ControlEntry.Seq = 0;
                     ControlEntry.SwitchingItem = 0;
                     ControlEntry.Application = Application$FMS;
                     ControlEntry.MoveEquipClass = Jobs[j].MoveEquipClass;
                     ControlEntry.PrintID = SelectEquip[i].NewPrintID;
                     ControlEntry.StepHeading = Jobs[j].StepPair;
                     ControlEntry.StepLevel = 0;
                     ControlEntry.TypeOfCard = DC.TypeOfCard; 

                     Status = Jobs[j].InsertControl (
                                     ControlEntry = ControlEntry
                                    ,InitiatingCard = DC.Card
                                    ,TransferFlag = TRUE
                                    ,SingleFeederOnly = TRUE
                                     );

                     IF Status = PU_CANCEL THEN
                       MESSAGE 'Procedure:TransferTo; Unable to establish ' +
                                'insert move control for the destination card.' +
                                SelectEquip[i].EquipName + ' has been transferred, ' + 
                                'the moves have not - contact Tech Support';

                       ENDLOOP;
                       RESUME; 
                     ENDIF; 

                     /* set the ActivityIdentifier to 'T' unless already shared or KPOS SB Equip */
                     IF Jobs[j].ActivityIdentifier <> 'S' AND Jobs[j].Equip <> KPS_SB.Equip THEN
                       CALLPROC SOA_JobActivityIDUpd (Job = Jobs[j].Job,
                                                   ActivityIdentifier = 'T');
                     ENDIF;
                     /*
                     ** Change Control Card for move if controlled by the previous card,
                     ** except for KPS_SB moves
                     */
                     IF Jobs[j].ControlCard = C.Card AND KPS_SB.Equip <> Jobs[j].Equip THEN
                       status = CALLPROC SOA_JobControlCardUpd (
                                               Job = Jobs[j].Job,
                                               Card = DC.Card);
                       IF status <> 0 THEN
                          CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                          MESSAGE 'Unable to change control card for move ' + 
                                  VARCHAR(Jobs[j].Job) + ' to the destination card. ' + 
                                  'Move might not be accessible - contact Tech Support.';
                       ENDIF;
                     ENDIF;
                     CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
                  ENDIF; 
               ENDIF; 
               j = j + 1; 
            ENDWHILE;
/*
** Update the jobs in the destination Card
*/        
            status = CALLPROC FMS_DestCardUpdate (
                                     DestinationCard = DC.Card,
                                     Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip);
    
            IF status < 0 THEN
              CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
              Message 'Unable to update the destination card to reflect ' +
                          'move transfers related to transferred ' +
                          'equipment.';
              ENDLOOP;
              RESUME;
            ELSE
              CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
              IF status > 0 THEN
                 message 'Because duplicate moves were transferred with this equipment,  ' +
                         'existing protection move links could not be resolved/' +
                         'transferred.  Please review your protection move links ' +
                         'on the Work Permits screen.';
              ENDIF;
            ENDIF;

            IF MacroEquip > 0 THEN
               status = CALLPROC FMS_DestCardUpdate (
                                     DestinationCard = DC.Card,
                                     Equip = MacroEquip);
    
              IF status < 0 THEN
                 CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                 Message 'Unable to update current card to reflect ' +
                          'move transfers related to macro equipment.';
                 ENDLOOP;
                 RESUME;
              ELSE
                 CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
                 IF status > 0 THEN
                    message 'Because duplicate moves were transferred with macro equipment,  ' +
                            'existing protection move links could not be resolved/' +
                            'transferred.  Please review your protection move links ' +
                            'on the Work Permits screen.';
                  ENDIF;
              ENDIF;
            ENDIF;
/*
** Remove any BT statuses
** related to this Jobclass and equipment
*/
            J = Jobs.LastRow();
       
            WHILE ( J  > 0 ) DO

               IF Jobs[J].StepPair = StepHeading$OTW THEN

                  IF Jobs[j].equip = SelectEquip[i].equip THEN

                       x = CALLPROC FMS_FromWorkStatusDel
                           (JobClass = Jobs[j].JobClass,
                            Equip = SelectEquip[i].Equip,
                            Job = 0,
                            Status = Status$BT,
                            Feeder = SelectEquip[i].Feeder);

                       IF x < 0 THEN
                          CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
                          Message 'Unable to clear BT feeder status.  Feeder Status List may be incorrect.';
                       ELSE
                          CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
                       ENDIF;                  

                  ENDIF;   

               ENDIF;

                 J = J - 1 ;   
            ENDWHILE;
         ENDIF;  /*KPS SB*/

         /* Log the transfer of equipment */ 
         CALLPROC SOA_LogIns 
	            ( Card = C.Card, 
	              Job  = NULL,        
	              Item = 'Xfer Equip', 
	              Old  = SelectEquip[i].PrintID + ' ' +
                             SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                             SelectEquip[i].EquipName,
	              New  = 'To ' + DC.FeederName,
                      Time = Date('now'),
                      UserName = UserName
                    ); 

         CALLPROC SOA_LogIns 
	            ( Card = DC.Card, 
	              Job  = NULL,        
	              Item = 'Xfer Equip', 
	              Old  = SelectEquip[i].PrintID + ' ' +
                             SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName + '  ' +
                             SelectEquip[i].EquipName,
	              New  = 'From ' + SelectEquip[i].FeederName,
                      Time = Date('now'),
                      UserName = UserName 
                     ); 
         CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
         /*
         **  Transfer SD Link if necessary.
         */
         CALLPROC SD_Transfer (SE = SelectEquip[i].Duplicate());
      ENDIF; 

      i = i + 1; 
   ENDWHILE;  
   CALLPROC MarkDiagramInvalid (Feeder = FeederObj, Feeder2 = DestinationFeeder);
/*
**    Handle remaining downstream from, look for Grouper on Target
*/   
      i = 1;
      SF6.Clear();
      REPEATED
      SELECT :SF6[i].PrimaryGrouping = O1.Object,
          :SF6[i].PrimaryGroupingName = O1.Name,
          :SF6[i].Object = O2.Object,
          :SF6[i].Name = O2.Name,
          :SF6[i].TypeName = O2.TypeName,
          :SF6[i].Description = O2.Description
      FROM   Udb_Object O1,
          Udb_Object O2,
          Udb_Grouping G
      WHERE  O2.Type IN       (SELECT Type
                            FROM  Udb_ExtendedType
                            WHERE  SuperType IN (:Type$DMSF6Switch,
                                                 :Type$DMEaton,
                                                 :Type$KPS,
                                                 :Type$FastSw,
                                                 :Type$DMVac) ) AND
          O2.Object = G.Member AND
          G.Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
          G.Grouping = :DestinationFeeder AND
          G.Grouping = O1.Object
      ORDER BY 2,5,4
      BEGIN 
         i = i + 1;
      END;

      FOR i = 1 TO DSF.LastRow DO
/*
** Find index in SelectList
*/
         FOR k = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow DO
             IF SelectEquip[k].Equip = DSF[i].Member THEN
                ENDLOOP;
             ENDIF;
         ENDFOR;

         j = 0;
         SELECT :j = Member
         FROM   Udb_Grouping 
         WHERE  Grouping = :DestinationFeeder AND
                Relationship = :Interaction$MemberOf AND
                Member = :DSF[i].Grouping;
/*
**    If it doesn't exist, delete it and look for another option
*/        
         IF j = 0 AND DSF[i].Member <> KPS_SB.Equip THEN
            x = CALLPROC Udb_GroupingDel (
                             Grouping = DSF[i].Grouping,
                             Relationship = Interaction$DownstreamFrom,
                             Member = DSF[i].Member);
            IF x < 0 THEN
               CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
               CALLPROC TraceError (UserMessage = '',
                                    TraceMessage = 'TransferFrom: Unable to clear DownStreamFrom ' +
                                                 'for Object ' + VARCHAR(DSF[i].Member));
            ELSE
               CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
               IF SF6.LastRow > 0 THEN
                  CALLFRAME KPISOSectionPrompt (Feeder = DestinationFeeder, 
                                       FeederName = DestinationFeederName,
                                       SF6 = SF6,
                                       Equip = DSF[i].Member,
                                       EquipName = SelectEquip[k].EquipName,
                                       EquipPrintID = SelectEquip[k].PrintID,
                                       EquipTypeName = SelectEquip[k].EquipClassName
                                      );
                  SelectEquip[k].IsAssigned = 99;
               ENDIF;
            ENDIF;  
         ELSE                
            SelectEquip[k].IsAssigned = 99;
         ENDIF;
      ENDFOR;   
/*
** If device downstreamfrom was not already handled and target feeder has SF6 option, then
** prompt to add Downstream From relationship.
*/      
      IF SF6.LastRow > 0 THEN
         FOR k = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow DO
           IF SelectEquip[k].IsAssigned <> 99 AND 
              FIELD(SelectEquip[k].Description).IsReverse = TRUE AND
              SelectEquip[k].Equip <> KPS_SB.Equip THEN
                   CALLFRAME KPISOSectionPrompt (Feeder = DestinationFeeder, 
                                       FeederName = DestinationFeederName,
                                       SF6 = SF6,
                                       Equip = SelectEquip[k].Equip,
                                       EquipName = SelectEquip[k].EquipName,
                                       EquipPrintID = SelectEquip[k].PrintID,
                                       EquipTypeName = SelectEquip[k].EquipClassName
                                      );
           ENDIF;
         ENDFOR;
      ENDIF;
/*
**    Adjust card header for both cards involved, just in case ground move or 
**    dead move was transferred.
*/
   IF EquipGrounded = TRUE THEN
         FOR k = 1 TO GroundFeeder.LastRow DO
            CALLPROC FMS_ManageCardHeader (OptionalFeeder = GroundFeeder[k].Value, Equip = 0);
            CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
         ENDFOR;
         CALLPROC FMS_ManageCardHeader (OptionalFeeder = DestinationFeeder, Equip = 0);
         CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
   ENDIF;

   IF DeadMove = TRUE THEN
      status = CALLPROC FMS_DeadMoveCount (Card = C.Card);
      IF status <> 0 THEN
         CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
         MESSAGE 'Dead Move Count on Old Card may not be correct due to an ' +
                 'error';
      ELSE
         CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
      ENDIF;
   ENDIF;

   IF entrymade < 2 THEN
      Message 'No Equipment to transfer.';
      RESUME;
   ENDIF;

/* notify impacted cards */
   FCFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'load_jobs');

   ControlText = VARCHAR(DC.Card) + ';' + UserName + ';';
   CALLPROC DDB_RaiseDBEvent ( DBEventName = 'SOA_NewJobOnCard', 
                               DBEventText = ControlText); 
   CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;

   RETURN PU_OK; 
END; 

/* 
**  Handle a Cancel click:  
*/ 
ON UserEvent 'ContinueCancel_Btn' = 
BEGIN 
	IF (entrymade > 0) THEN 
	  IF (CurFrame.ConfirmPopup(messagetext= 
	      'Equipment will not be transferred.  Continue?') = PU_OK 
	     ) THEN 
	    RETURN PU_CANCEL;  
	  ENDIF; 
	ELSE 
	  IF (CurFrame.ConfirmPopup(messagetext= 
	      'Equipment Transfer is cancelled.  Continue?') = PU_OK ) THEN
	     RETURN PU_CANCEL;
          ENDIF; 
	ENDIF; 
END; 

/* 
**  Handle the Close Window Command: 
*/ 
ON WINDOWCLOSE = 
BEGIN 
   RESUME; 
END; 

PROCEDURE UpdateSelectedList(
) =
DECLARE
   i        = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   k        = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   TempEquipList = ARRAY OF FMS_Equip;
ENDDECLARE
BEGIN
   TempEquipList.Clear();
   k = 1;
   FOR i = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow DO
      IF Field(SelectEquip[i].Origin).IsReverse = TRUE THEN
         TempEquipList[k] = SelectEquip[i].Duplicate();
         k = k + 1;
      ENDIF;
   ENDFOR;
   SelectedEquip = TempEquipList.Duplicate(); 
END;

PROCEDURE RFP_Link (
   Object    = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   IsReverse = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   Card      = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   LinkID    = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
) =
DECLARE
   i        = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   k        = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   TempEquip = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   RFPList  = ARRAY OF IR_RequestForPermit;
   RFPEquip = ARRAY OF INTEGEROBJECT;
   YesDO    = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   YesFCR   = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   RetCode   = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   UserMessage = VARCHAR(1000) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT; /*Optional*/
ENDDECLARE
BEGIN
   IF IsReverse = FALSE THEN  /* UnSelect row */
      IF LinkID <> 0 THEN
         FOR i = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow DO
            IF SelectEquip[i].G = LinkID THEN
               FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Origin).IsReverse = IsReverse;
               FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Description).IsReverse = IsReverse;
               FIELD(SelectEquip[i].PrintID).IsReverse = IsReverse;
               FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipName).IsReverse = IsReverse;
               FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName).IsReverse = IsReverse;
               SelectEquip[i].G = 0;  /* Clear field */
            ENDIF;
         ENDFOR;
      ENDIF;
      CALLPROC UpdateSelectedList();
      RETURN;
   ENDIF;

   /* Row Selected */
   i =1;
   RFPList.Clear();
   SELECT DISTINCT
          RFPList[i].RFP = R.RFP,
          RFPList[i].LinkedByDO = R.LinkedByDO
   FROM   SOA_JobControl JC,
          SOA_Job J,
          SOA_Job J2,
          FMS_WorkPermitProtection WPP,
          IR_WorkLocation WL,
          IR_RequestForPermit R
   WHERE  JC.Card = :Card AND
          JC.Job  = J.Job AND
          J.Equip = :Object AND
          J.Job  = WPP.ProtectionJobID AND
          WPP.PermitJobId = WL.WorkPermit AND
          WPP.PermitJobId = J2.Job AND
          J2.TOIssued IS NULL AND
          WL.RFP = R.RFP
   BEGIN
      i = i + 1;
   END;
   CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
      
   IF RFPList.LastRow = 0 THEN
      CALLPROC UpdateSelectedList();
      RETURN;
   ENDIF;
   
   FOR i = 1 TO RFPList.LastRow DO
      IF RFPList[i].LinkedByDO = TRUE THEN
         YesDO = TRUE;
      ELSE
         YesFCR = TRUE;
      ENDIF;
   ENDFOR;
   
   IF YesFCR = TRUE THEN
      IF YesFCRWarning = 0 THEN
         RetCode = CALLFRAME ConfirmThreeChoice(pTitle = 'RFP Link Check'
                                ,pConfirmText = 
              'This piece of equipment has a move defined as a protection ' + 
              'move for a work permit that has an RFP that was NOT linked ' +
              'to the card by a DO.' + HC_NEWLINE + HC_NEWLINE + 
              'If you transfer this equipment to the Known Point ISO ' + 
              'card the RFP and associated work permit will not be ' + 
              'transferred to the KPI card.' + HC_NEWLINE + HC_NEWLINE + 
              'Select ''Confirm'' to override this warning and transfer ' + 
              'equipment anyway.'
                                ,pbtn1text = 'Confirm'
                                ,pbtn2text = 'Cancel'
                                ,pBGColor = CC_RED
                                ,pFGColor = CC_WHITE
                                );
         IF RetCode = 2 THEN
            FIELD(SelectEquip[].Origin).IsReverse = FALSE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[].Description).IsReverse = FALSE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[].PrintID).IsReverse = FALSE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipName).IsReverse = FALSE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipClassName).IsReverse = FALSE;
      
            CALLPROC UpdateSelectedList();
            RETURN;
         ENDIF;
         YesFCRWarning = 1;
      ENDIF;
      CALLPROC UpdateSelectedList();
      RETURN;
   ENDIF;
   
   IF YesDO = TRUE THEN
      RFPEquip.Clear();
      FOR i = 1 TO RFPList.LastRow DO
         SELECT DISTINCT
                TempEquip = J.Equip
         FROM   IR_WorkLocation WL,
                FMS_WorkPermitProtection WPP,
                SOA_Job J,
                SOA_Job J2,
                SOA_JobControl JC
         WHERE  WL.RFP = :RFPList[i].RFP AND
                WL.WorkPermit = WPP.PermitJobID AND
                WPP.PermitJobID = J2.Job AND
                J2.TOIssued IS NULL AND
                WPP.ProtectionJobID = J.Job AND
                J.Job = JC.Job AND
                JC.Card = :Card
         BEGIN
            FOR k = 1 TO RFPEquip.LastRow DO
               IF RFPEquip[k].Value = TempEquip THEN
                  ENDLOOP;
               ENDIF;
            ENDFOR;
            IF k > RFPEquip.LastRow THEN
               RFPEquip[k].Value = TempEquip;
            ENDIF;
         END;
         CALLPROC DDB_ROLLBACK;
      ENDFOR;
      
      IF RFPEquip.LastRow > 1 AND YesDOWarning = 0 THEN
         RetCode = CALLFRAME ConfirmThreeChoice(pTitle = 'RFP Link Check'
                                ,pConfirmText = 
              'This equipment has a work permit protection move ' + 
              'for a DO linked RFP. ' + HC_NEWLINE + HC_NEWLINE +
              'All equipment that is a protection ' +  
              'move for this RFP will be transferred to the Known Point Iso. ' + HC_NEWLINE + HC_NEWLINE + 
              'Select ''Confirm'' to highlight other equipment for transfer.'
                                ,pbtn1text = 'Confirm'
                                ,pbtn2text = 'Cancel'
                                );
         IF RetCode = 2 THEN
            FIELD(SelectEquip[].Origin).IsReverse = FALSE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[].Description).IsReverse = FALSE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[].PrintID).IsReverse = FALSE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipName).IsReverse = FALSE;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[].EquipClassName).IsReverse = FALSE;

            CALLPROC UpdateSelectedList();
            RETURN;
         ENDIF;
         YesDOWarning = 1;     
      ENDIF;
      
      i = 1;
      FOR i = 1 TO 10 DO
         k = 0;
         k = SelectEquip.Find(AttributeName = 'G',
                              VALUE = i);
         IF k = ER_ROWNOTFOUND THEN
            LinkID = i; /* Group all equipment together for de-select later */
            ENDLOOP;
         ENDIF;
      ENDFOR;
      
      FOR i = 1 TO RFPEquip.LastRow DO
         FOR k = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow DO
            IF SelectEquip[k].Equip = RFPEquip[i].Value THEN
               FIELD(SelectEquip[k].Origin).IsReverse = TRUE;
               FIELD(SelectEquip[k].Description).IsReverse = TRUE;
               FIELD(SelectEquip[k].PrintID).IsReverse = TRUE;
               FIELD(SelectEquip[k].EquipName).IsReverse = TRUE;
               FIELD(SelectEquip[k].EquipClassName).IsReverse = TRUE;
               SelectEquip[k].G = LinkID;
            ENDIF;
         ENDFOR; 
      ENDFOR;     
   ENDIF;
   
   CALLPROC UpdateSelectedList();
   RETURN;
END;

PROCEDURE SD_Link (
   Object    = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   IsReverse = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   Type      = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
) =
DECLARE
   i         = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   SDObject  = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
ENDDECLARE
BEGIN 
   /*
   **  Check to see if this is a type we are interested in.
   */
   SDObject = 0;
   IF Type = Type$StepDown THEN  /* SD-TRANSF */
      /*
      **  Find paired piece of equipment
      */
      SELECT :SDObject = G.Member
      FROM    Udb_Grouping G
      WHERE   G.Grouping = :Object AND
              G.Relationship = :Interaction$LocatedWith AND
              G.MemberType = :Type$SDVIS;
   ELSEIF Type = Type$SDVIS THEN
      /*
      **  Find paired piece of equipment
      */
      SELECT :SDObject = G.Grouping
      FROM    Udb_Grouping G
      WHERE   G.Member = :Object AND
              G.Relationship = :Interaction$LocatedWith AND
              G.GroupingType = :Type$StepDown;
   ENDIF;
   
   IF SDObject <> 0 THEN 
      FOR i = 1 TO SelectEquip.LastRow DO
         IF SelectEquip[i].Equip = SDObject THEN
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Origin).IsReverse = IsReverse;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].Description).IsReverse = IsReverse;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].PrintID).IsReverse = IsReverse;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipName).IsReverse = IsReverse;
            FIELD(SelectEquip[i].EquipClassName).IsReverse = IsReverse;
 
            RETURN;
         ENDIF;
      ENDFOR;
   ENDIF;
          
   RETURN;
END;

PROCEDURE SD_Transfer (
   SE = FMS_Equip;
) =
DECLARE
   SDCard  = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   Card    = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
ENDDECLARE
BEGIN 
   /*
   **  Only check when SDVIS device is being transferred.
   */
   IF SE.EquipClass <> Type$SDVIS THEN
      RETURN;
   ENDIF;
   /*
   **  Only transfer links for 27kV cards.
   */
   IF C.TypeOfCard = TypeOfCard$4KV THEN
      RETURN;
   ENDIF;
   /*
   **  Find the StepDown card that this equipment is on.
   */
   Card = 0;
   SELECT :SDCard = L.StepDownCard,
          :Card = L.Card
   FROM    Udb_Grouping G,
           SOA_ActiveObject AO,
           FMS_StepDownLink L
   WHERE   G.Member = :SE.Equip AND
           G.Relationship = :Interaction$SourceBreaker AND
           G.Grouping = AO.Object AND
           AO.Card = L.StepDownCard;

   IF Card <> 0 THEN
      CALLPROC FMS_StepDownLinkUpd
          (OldCard = Card,
           Card = DC.Card,                   
           OldStepDownCard = SDCard,
           StepDownCard = 0);   /* Triggers update of Card */
      CALLPROC DDB_COMMIT;
      FCFrame.SendUserEvent (EventName = 'RefreshCardLinks');          
   ENDIF;         
   RETURN;
END;

PROCEDURE MTA_Check (
) =
DECLARE
   i  = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   j  = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   RowFound  = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   GridEquip = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   GridRow = INTEGER NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
   XEquip = ARRAY OF INTEGEROBJECT;
   UnselectedRow = ARRAY OF INTEGEROBJECT;
   MessageText = VARCHAR(500) NOT NULL WITH DEFAULT;
ENDDECLARE
BEGIN 
   /*
   **  Only check when MTA or Microgrid equipment are being transferred.
   */
   GridEquip = 0;
   SELECT :GridEquip = Member
   FROM    Udb_Grouping
   WHERE   Grouping = :FeederObj AND
           Relationship IN (:Interaction$MTAIsolationFor,
                            :Interaction$MicroGridGenFor,
                            :Interaction$MicroGridFor);
   IF GridEquip = 0 THEN
      RETURN;
   ENDIF;
   
   i = 0;
   RowFound = SelectEquip.Find(AttributeName = 'Equip',
                             Value = GridEquip,
                             RowNumber = BYREF(GridRow) );
   IF RowFound = ER_OK THEN
      IF FIELD(SelectEquip[GridRow].Origin).IsReverse = FALSE THEN
         RETURN;   /* Not selected */
      ENDIF;
   ENDIF;
   /*
   ** MTA or Microgrid equipment is being transferred, look at downstream equip
   */
   XEquip.Clear();
   i = 1;
   SELECT DISTINCT
          XEquip[i].Value = G.Member
   FROM   Udb_Grouping G
   WHERE  G.Grouping = :GridEquip AND
          G.Relationship IN (:Interaction$DownstreamFrom,:Interaction$MTADownstreamOf)
   BEGIN
      i = i + 1;
   END;

   UnselectedRow.Clear();
   i = XEquip.LastRow;
   WHILE i >=1 DO
      j = 0; 
      RowFound = SelectEquip.Find(AttributeName = 'Equip',
                             Value = XEquip[i].Value,
                             RowNumber = BYREF(j) );
      IF RowFound = ER_OK THEN
         IF FIELD(SelectEquip[j].Origin).IsReverse = FALSE THEN
            UnselectedRow.InsertRow (Rownumber = 1);
            UnselectedRow[1].Value = j;
         ENDIF;
      ENDIF;
      i = i - 1;      
   ENDWHILE;
   
   IF UnselectedRow.LastRow = 0 THEN
      RETURN;  /* All downstream from equip selected */
   ENDIF;
   
   FOR i = 1 TO UnselectedRow.LastRow DO
      IF i > 1 THEN
         MessageText = MessageText + ', ' + HC_NEWLINE;
      ENDIF;
      j = UnselectedRow[i].Value;
      MessageText = MessageText + '  ' + SelectEquip[j].EquipClassName + ' ' + SelectEquip[j].EquipName;
   ENDFOR;
   
   IF CurFrame.ConfirmPopup (MessageText = 'These equipment are marked downstream from ' + 
               SelectEquip[GridRow].EquipClassName + ' ' + SelectEquip[GridRow].EquipName +
               ':' + HC_NEWLINE + MessageText + HC_NEWLINE + HC_NEWLINE + 'Should they be included in the transfer?') = PU_CANCEL THEN
      RETURN;
   ELSE
      FOR i = 1 TO UnselectedRow.LastRow DO
         j = UnselectedRow[i].Value;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[j].Origin).IsReverse = TRUE;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[j].Description).IsReverse = TRUE;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[j].PrintID).IsReverse = TRUE;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[j].EquipName).IsReverse = TRUE;
         FIELD(SelectEquip[j].EquipClassName).IsReverse = TRUE;
      ENDFOR;  
   ENDIF;
   RETURN;
END;
